\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Off highs, on yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears. \b0\par\par\uc2 863 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 2003\par 04:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Jan 16 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar\par and Thai baht  stayed away from their multi-month highs\par early on Thursday as Asia regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market focused on\par the threat of Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to halt the yen's\par climb.\par     Dealers said while price action in the dollar/yen was\par relatively muted and sentiment still bearish on the greenback,\par fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in aid of the wobbly U.S. dollar prompted\par players to book profits on recent gains in regionals.\par     Japan's new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief Zembei Mizoguchi repeated his\par mantra that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market moves could become excessive and the\par finance ministry would be closely monitoring for such moves.\par  \par     The dollar/yen was within a narrow 118.03-118.24 range in\par quiet trade, compared with late New York level of 118.11/19.\par     The dollar fell as low as 117.77 yen in post-Asian trade on\par Wednesday due to weak U.S. stocks amid worries about corporate\par earnings as reporting season heats up.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Expression of bearish sentiment on dollar was more\par pronounced in the euro that was well-supported at around\par $1.0552/55  against $1.0549/54 in New York.\par     The Singapore dollar        was around 1.7328 per U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, stronger than an early session low of 1.7345 and late\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday's 1.7348 but off six-month highs beyond the 1.7300\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level hit on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said most players covered short U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions and some genuine dollar demand from local corporates\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was also capping the Sing dollar's upside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par DATA WATCH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, dealers said players were cautiously watching for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par any surprises in Singapore December non-oil domestic exports\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par data due on Friday, after data on Wednesday showed the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par city-state's retail sales posted their strongest rise in eight\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par months in November. Sales climbed by a stronger-than-expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 7.3 percent from October as shoppers snapped up big-ticket\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par items ahead of a consumption tax rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bhanu Baweja, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS Warburg in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore, said the unexpected rise could be explained in terms\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of consumers trying to beat the GST tax hike.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     He said a possible shift in tourism to Singapore after the\par October 12 Bali bombing might also be a factor.\par     He said, however, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains were likely to be\par moderate.\par     "We maintain that Sing dollar is likely to appreciate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par through the year, but the gains are likely to be the smallest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par amongst all Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as economic risk from slow exports\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and an increasingly more competitive Malaysian ringgit peg puts\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pressure," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Weakness in the U.S. dollar has helped \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  like the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ringgit, pegged to the dollar at 3.80 per U.S. dollar since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1998, in terms of real effective exchange rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BAHT EYES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht  was around 42.70 per dollar, against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par late Wednesday's 42.63 and a four-month high of 42.54 on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said players unwound long baht positions on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , spotted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in recent sessions, was to cap baht's gains and protect export\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par competitiveness, they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers expect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to continue bidding for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars around 42.50 level, despite overall bullish sentiment\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on on a buoyant domestic economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  actively manages the baht to iron out\par volatility but has no declared target level for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Jocelyn Pang, an economist at DBS Bank in Singapore, said\par the baht was likely to stay supported around 42-43 range\par through early 2003.\par     "Growing employment and wages, a robust housing sector, and\par fiscal spending will continue to support domestic demand for\par much of 2003," she said in a recent research report.\par     The Philippine peso        was holding around 53.50 per\par U.S. dollar, after hitting this week's lowest level at 53.545.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        was around 8,860 per U.S.\par dollar, slightly stronger on the day as dollar sales from\par foreign banks absorbed dollar purchases from state-run firms.\par     The Taiwan dollar          stepped back from the two-month\par highs hit on Wednesday. For a detailed report,\par     The South Korean won                   was off six-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par high hit on Wednesday, but was seen supported by dollar sales\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from offshore players. For a detailed report,\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0256 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.23       118.13         -0.08\par  Sing dlr      1.7323       1.7348         +0.14\par  Taiwan dlr    34.475       34.490         +0.04\par  Korean won   1173.40      1175.40         +0.17\par  Baht           42.66        42.63         -0.07\par  Peso           53.52        53.48         -0.07\par  Rupiah       8862.00      8870.00         +0.09\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.23       118.74         +0.43\par  Sing dlr      1.7323       1.7341         +0.10\par  Taiwan dlr    34.475       34.753         +0.81\par  Korean won   1173.40      1185.80         +1.06\par  Baht           42.66        43.08    