\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  fears restrict gains. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Vidya Ranganathan \par \uc2 749 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 2003\par 05:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 15 (Reuters) - Fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  held back Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday after they hit multi-month highs on heightened risks of war and rising pessimism on the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar and Korean won hesitated at six-month highs, the Thai baht failed to go past four-month highs and the Taiwan dollar stayed near two-month highs. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar hit a four-month low against the yen  and a fresh\par three-year low against the euro        after weaker than expected U.S.\par retail data and reports U.N. weapons inspectors found evidence Iraq had\par smuggled arms-related goods.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the dollar bounced back above 118 yen after the new Japanese Vice\par Finance Minister for International Affairs, Zembei Mizoguchi, warned\par Japan would take action against excessive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There remains a widespread perception in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets that the\par Bank of Japan will not be keen on seeing dollar-yen below 118 and\par that's holding up the dollar up,"said Sameer Goel, strategist at Bank\par of America, adding that the loss of momentum in the rallying yen had\par reined in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par YEN A BIG FACTOR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Most regional central banks think about their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par trade-weighted terms and Japan is an important component in those\par baskets. The markets would be comfortable driving Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par higher against the dollar as long as that is the trend which is\par followed by the euro and yen," Goel said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar  hit a five-month high of 1.7297 per U.S. dollar\par in offshore trade before giving up most gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But, given the U.S. dollar's lingering weakness, traders no longer\par feared it was nearing the limits of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's undisclosed\par trade-weighted band, within which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is managed.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Korean won             touched 1,171 per U.S. dollar but then pared\par some of its gains after a finance ministry comment that the strength\par was excessive.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The current spot level is approaching 2002's (dollar) low of 1,165, a\par support that is unlikely to be broken without a fight from Korean\par officials, given lingering uncertainties in the external environment,"\par JP Morgan said in a market commentary.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar  rose past a key resistance at 34.50 per U.S. dollar\par to hit 34.45 and then stalled as traders anticipated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . They said the authorities \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  the previous day.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FEARS CAP BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht's gains were capped at the previous day's highs of 42.60\par per U.S. dollar. Reports of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the\par dollar if it strengthened beyond 42.60 could not be confirmed. Traders\par said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  normally \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through other banks in\par offshore markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah  was relatively steady in a range of 8,860-8,875\par per U.S. dollar, near a one-month high, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market brushed\par off ongoing protests against price hikes and focused on IMF aid\par meetings next week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia's international donors will meet on January 21-22 to discuss\par fresh aid pledges with the government.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Jakarta-based traders said most of the dollar sales were by the bullish\par offshore players.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Rupiah is remarkably resilient below 8,900 as investor interest to\par receive carry remains high. Offshore yields are now at par with the\par onshore rates, reflecting increased foreign investor appetite to be\par short dollars," JP Morgan said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso  underperformed, staying flat just off a one-week\par high of 53.35 per dollar while neighbours' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0335 GMT Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen     118.22       119.20         +0.83\par   Sing dlr      1.7331       1.7341         +0.06\par   Taiwan dlr    34.473       34.528         +0.16\par   Korean won   1173.20      1176.60         +0.29\par   Baht           42.64        42.64         +0.00\par   Peso           53.42        53.39         -0.06\par   Rupiah       8865.00      8865.00         +0.00\par   Change on year\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par   Japan yen     118.22       118.74         +0.44\par   Sing dlr      1.7331       1.7341         +0.06\par   Taiwan dlr    34.473       34.753         +0.81\par   Korean won   1173.20      1185.80         +1.07\par   Baht           42.64        43.08         +1.03\par   Peso           53.42        53.38         -0.07\par   Rupiah       8865.00      8940.00         +0.85.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030115dz1f0081a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
