\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK \highlight\uc2  WATCH: Singapore MAS Policy Likely Neutral \b0\par\par\uc2  By Izham Ahmad \par \uc2 913 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Dezember 2002\par 08:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Although Singapore's economic growth faltered somewhat in the second half of this year, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't expected to switch to an easier monetary policy any time soon. \par \par \uc2  When it unveils its half-yearly policy plans next week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore is widely expected to stick to its current neutral stance. \par \par \uc2  Economists said that it will likely adopt this position, considering the current policy remains accommodative enough for an economy that has been growing by fits and starts, and which isn't expected to pick up speed till the second half. Inflation, meanwhile, is largely absent. \par \par \uc2  However, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Singapore dollar, has appreciated against the U.S. dollar, and could pose some risks for the trade-dependent economy. \par \par \uc2  The local dollar's resurgence comes against a backdrop of a broadly weaker U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In recent weeks, the U.S. dollar has weakened amid concerns over whether the current administration remains as committed to a strong dollar policy, as well as on fears related to the growing tensions between the U.S. and Iraq. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore will announce its policy stance at 0000 GMT Jan. 2. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  implements monetary policy by weakening or strengthening the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an undisclosed band against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its major trading partners. \par \par \uc2  "An explicit depreciating policy risks instability and can be ruled out," Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi said in a research report published Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The MAS eased monetary policy to neutral eighteen months ago and has since then twice affirmed it. It has, however, adjusted the undisclosed band twice. \par \par \uc2  Allowing the Singapore dollar to trade within a broader range was taken as a signal to the markets that the MAS was more willing to tolerate a weaker local dollar, even though that wasn't considered an outright depreciation. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore economy contracted 2% last year. Despite a promising start in the new year, the economy continues to struggle to fully recover. The government expects gross domestic product growth to expand between 2% and 2.5% this year - sharply lower than earlier forecast. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    3Q GDP Shrank Vs 2Q\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Throughout the whole of 2002, they (MAS) insisted they wouldn't use\par the exchange rate to boost exports, I don't see why, now that things are\par starting to look a little better, they would deviate from that\par position," said Joseph Tan, an economist at Standard Chartered Bank in\par Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A neutral stance also accommodates the government's view that the\par economy will continue to recover next year, though that growth would\par still be meek until the second half when the economy should begin to\par pick up strength.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There were some fears earlier the economy could slip back into\par recession following a quarterly contraction in the July-September\par period, but recent data suggest otherwise. An unexpected 19%\par year-on-year surge in non-oil domestic exports in November, for\par instance, suggested the economy has regained some strength and that the\par final quarter of the year will likely see GDP growing again.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Prices have begun to rise, after a period of persistent deflation. In\par any case, inflationary pressures aren't a real concern at this time. In\par November, the consumer price index, the most commonly used measure of\par inflation in the republic, rose 0.2% over the year - the first\par year-on-year rise since June. Indeed, the MAS doesn't expect the 2002\par CPI to differ much from last year's rate by more than 50 basis points\par either way.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Things are starting to stabilize. We are seeing some signs of life. I\par think all the talk of a double-dip recession has been over-hyped," said\par Sim Moh Siong, economist at Salomon Smith Barney/Citicorp.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, the Singapore dollar has gained some 4.5% since October\par against the U.S. dollar without apparently drawing any disapproving\par growls from the republic's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The MAS is believed to\par have occasionally \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to iron out any excessively sharp moves in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar. It is believed to favor a weaker local dollar at\par the moment to keep exports competitive.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But Jimmy Koh, head of treasury research at United Overseas Bank Ltd.\par (P.UOB), pointed out that on a trade-weighted basis, the Singapore\par dollar has been flat, and that given the state of the economy, "could\par very well underperform vis-a-vis the other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (by\par year-end)."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Around 0745 GMT Thursday, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7370\par compared with S$1.7387, near the end of Tuesday's shortened Asian\par trading session. Markets were closed Wednesday for Christmas.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Other analysts noted that even with the gains, the Singapore dollar\par remains within the MAS's undisclosed policy range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Other than the explicit policy statement, analysts would also be\par scrutinizing the tone of MAS' statement, which usually accompanies the\par policy announcement, for an update of the economic situation. Economic\par data up to December should be available, giving the authority some\par indication of whether the pickup in the economy in November has\par continued - or stumbled again.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Emmanuel Ng, an economist at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi, said that\par "they'll probably say (in the accompanying statement) that it (Singapore\par dollar exchange rate) remains accommodative of the ongoing recovery."\par    -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-64154-157;\par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1184 4253 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020021226dycq000bp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
