\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Singapore dollar at 5-month high. \b0\par\par\uc2 450 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 2002\par 04:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Dec 24 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar  rose to a fresh five-month high on Tuesday, extending the previous day's yen-driven rally in thin holiday trade. \par \par \uc2  While verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities and the mounting risk of a U.S-led attack on Iraq hemmed the dollar within a narrow 120.30-120.50 range against the yen, off an overnight one-month low of 119.83, the Singapore dollar continued rising after a brief corrective dip. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said there is a need to keep watching purchasing power parity and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, and that rapid moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates must be prevented. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa has earlier said the yen should be at 150 to the dollar as per the purchasing power parity, which compares living standards among nations. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar hit a fresh five-month high of 1.7380 and quoted at 1.7380/90 after the morning's drop to 1.7412. \par \par \uc2  "This is quite surprising, given the market is quite worried about the trade-weighted band and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 -based trader said. \par \par \uc2  "But I guess this is a result of stop-losses and thin liquidity." \par \par \uc2  Bank dealing rooms were thinly staffed on Christmas Eve, especially with regional markets in Indonesia and Philippines closed for the holiday. \par \par \uc2  Local markets have been wary of pushing the Sing dollar higher for fear it will become overvalued in trade-weighted terms just days before the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) announces its twice-yearly review of monetary policy on January 2. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar is up nearly three cents so far in December and has benefitted from a recent batch of healthier economic data and the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  The MAS makes public its policy bias but never discloses the parameters of the band within which it guides the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It targets the Singapore dollar's trade-weighted nominal effective exchange rate and keeps the value within this secret band. \par \par \uc2  The last time the MAS issued a monetary policy statement was in July, when it reaffirmed its neutral policy stance on the Singapore dollar . The Thai baht  tailed the Sing dollar at a leisurely pace, hugging the 43 level. \par \par \uc2  Trading volumes were low but \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers waited for a likely hedging interest from oil importers after the risk of war and the prolonged strike in Venezuela pushed oil prices to a two-year high. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar  merely followed the yen, giving up Monday's high of 34.818 as the yen buckled to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears. For the detailed report, \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Korean won             came off 1,198 and steadied around 1,200.\par For a detailed report,.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021224dyco0066c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
