\par\par \b \uc2  Informal MAS talks broach Sing dlr competitiveness. \b0\par\par\uc2 468 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2002\par 11:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Dec 20 (Reuters) - Some economists consulted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore have floated the idea of a weaker Singapore dollar as an antidote to deflationary pressures, a local academic said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Chen Kang, an associate professor at Nanyang Technological University, said the question of a weaker dollar was discussed at informal talks he attended on Thursday at the invitation of Koh Yong Guan, the MAS's managing director. \par \par \uc2  "We did talk about this issue of a lower Sing dollar," Chen told a conference organised by the Institute of Policy Studies, a Singapore think tank. \par \par \uc2  "Some people mentioned that this could be an alternative... given the global environment of a deflationary situation," said Chen, head of the applied economics division at the university's business school. \par \par \uc2  "But the problem of how to do it is quite dangerous. If you try to lower the Sing dollar and the market pushes for it, there will be no end to it. So implementation is the most difficult part," he added. \par \par \uc2  Chen was speaking at the presentation of a report the IPS has submitted to the government on ways of revitalising Singapore's economy. \par \par \uc2  Asked to comment, the MAS said: "MAS has met with some economists from the private and public sectors to discuss recent economic developments and outlook for the economy. \par \par \uc2  "This is part of MAS's ongoing efforts to engage in public consultation and to enhance our surveillance of the economy. The discussion was informal and centred on macroeconomic issues, including monetary policy." \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar this week hit 1.7419 per U.S. dollar, the highest level since September 4, but dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets had been reluctant to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher for fear of provoking \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the MAS. \par \par \uc2  The MAS, \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , conducts monetary policy by targeting the exchange rate rather than interest rates to protect the small export-oriented economy from the disruption of major capital flows. \par \par \uc2  To run the policy, the MAS manages the value of the Singapore dollar against a weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its key trading partners such as the United States, Europe, Japan and Malaysia. \par \par \uc2  It targets the Singapore dollar's trade-weighted nominal effective exchange rate and keeps the value within a secret range or policy band. \par \par \uc2  Another speaker at the IPS conference said Singapore should actively consider the option of weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the domestic sector of the economy. \par \par \uc2  Tan Kin Lian, chief executive officer of National Trades Union Congress's Income Insurance Cooperative Ltd, said the Singapore dollar had appreciated significantly in recent years against regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "This is the main cause of our uncompetitiveness. Our customers in the region now find it too expensive to use our services," Tan said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021220dyck00idh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
