\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Modest gains as dlr bows to war threat. \b0\par\par\uc2 827 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2002\par 09:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Dec 20 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose marginally on Friday, benefitting as the U.S. dollar's weakened on heightening fears of a war against Iraq, but they lacked any real conviction in the move. \par \par \uc2  The dollar weakened to under 121 yen after the United States said Iraq was in "material breach" of the U.N. resolution on weapons inspections, raising worries of a war, although U.S. officials said an attack is not imminent. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was the main beneficiary of the U.S. dollar's weakness as the other regionals grappled with local factors. \par \par \uc2  Traders were also reluctant to take strong views on the yen, a dominant factor for the regionals, as confusion again reigned over what Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy was. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said the authorities were not thinking about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the yen, after authoring a newspaper article saying the yen was overvalued and his ministry would take appropriate action if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Minutes of the Bank of Japan's November meeting also revealed \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  calls for unsterilised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a meeting last month, a move which could weaken the yen. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso stayed near the week's lows at 53.72-53.75, although fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  curbed losses. Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this week when the peso hit three-week lows. \par \par \uc2  Keenly awaited figures showed the budget deficit for the 11 months to November topping 200 billion pesos, but it may beat the 2002 target of 223 billion - although this has been revised up three times from an original target of 130 billion pesos. \par \par \uc2  Despite revenues beating their target for the first time this year, analysts remained bearish on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  SING DOLLAR REINED IN, BAHT PRESSURED \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar rallied offshore to a 3-= month high of 1.7419 before Asian traders, concerned it will become too strong in trade-weighted terms and wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , shaved some of the gains. \par \par \uc2  The MAS does not disclose the trade-weighted band it targets, but market estimates have the Sing at the strong end of the band. \par \par \uc2  "It is 0.25 percent away from the upper end of the band and there's always a risk that if this move is overdone the MAS will come in," Bhanu Baweja, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg said. \par \par \uc2  The Korean won was slightly weaker despite the higher yen as onshore markets waited for the ruling party's president-elect Roh Moo-hyun to announce his policies. \par \par \uc2  Since winning Thursday's election, Roh has said he will make effort to stem the rises in consumer and property prices and has called for a mature relationship with the United States. \par \par \uc2  The won has not kept pace with the yen's rally from 125.70 two weeks ago, evidenced in the rising yen-won cross rate. \par \par \uc2  The cross rate is now quoted at 9.97, up from 9.61 at the start of December. Markets believe the Korean authorities are comfortable with a level of 10 to ensure the won's competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  "Although there are some big positives in Korea, the government is still, and quite legitimately, worried about competitiveness in a situation that's already quite bad for the external sector," Baweja said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht could not hold on to a high of 42.95 as offshore banks covered short dollar-baht positions in the final trading days of 2002. \par \par \uc2  A Bangkok-based trader said offshore banks had been selling dollars for more than two weeks hoping for baht appreciation, but local importers kept a lid on the upside. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar also to make gains, but closed just above Thursday's 34.885 close, as markets overcame a Standard & Poor's sovereign rating downgrade earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah held a familiar 8,875-8,890 range, awaiting foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows from PT Astra International's rights issue and further bad loan sales by Indonesia's Bank Restructuring Agency. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0809 GMT\par   Change on the day\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen     120.79       121.11         +0.26\par   Sing dlr      1.7434       1.7455         +0.12\par   Taiwan dlr    34.853       34.885         +0.09\par   Korean won   1204.70      1201.00         -0.31\par   Baht           43.06        42.97         -0.21\par   Peso           53.60        53.75         +0.28\par   Rupiah       8885.00      8870.00         -0.17\par   Change on year\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par   Japan yen     120.79       131.24         +8.65\par   Sing dlr      1.7434       1.8515         +6.20\par   Taiwan dlr    34.853       34.986