\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Looking for direction, peso weak. \b0\par\par\uc2 814 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2002\par 10:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Dec 19 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  struggled\par for direction on Thursday as markets dithered over conflicting\par signals on the U.S. dollar, with the Philippine peso setting a\par three-week low ahead of a budget deficit update.\par     After reclaiming 121 yen in early deals, the U.S. dollar\par was largely unmoved in Asia as markets fretted over America's\par build-up of troops in preparation for possible action on Iraq.\par     The inertia was partly on account of Wednesday's White\par House affirmation of its strong-dollar policy and the confusion\par over which way Japanese authorities want the yen to head --\par finance ministry rhetoric favours a weak yen but ruling Liberal\par Democratic Party members have echoed the Bank of Japan's view\par that a strong yen was not a bad thing.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The mood is clearly dollar-bearish, but because of all the\par badgering by the Japanese authorities on the yen, there has\par been little movement in regionals today," Sameer Goel,\par strategist with Bank of America, said.\par     The Philippine peso hit a three week low of 53.80 per\par dollar in late trade, after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor denied\par the bank had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the peso on Thursday -- talk\par which had earlier helped the peso off its morning lows.\par     Traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also thought to have\par supported the peso on Tuesday and Wednesday. The peso has been\par plagued by worries over the burgeoning fiscal deficit, and data\par for the 11 months to November is expected on Friday.\par      A government source told Reuters the deficit would be\par around 200 billion pesos, close to the revised 223 billion\par pesos or 5.6 percent of GDP target set for the whole year. The\par original target was a full-year deficit of 130 billion pesos.\par     "We are approaching the last trading day (of 2002) which is\par December 27, so no one is taking aggressive positions and small\par flows are causing exaggerated moves," a Manila-based trader\par said.\par     "I guess most traders will feel comfortable during this\par holiday only if they go home with a slightly long dollar book,"\par he said, referring to the persistent bearishness on the peso.\par  \par     Despite the gloom, the peso was little moved by data\par showing a shrinking trade surplus and balance of payments.\par     The trade surplus fell 24.7 percent in the January-October\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par period from a year earlier. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said the balance\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of payments in the nine months to September was in surplus by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $751 million, down from $903 million at the end of August.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BAHT STEADY, KOREA SHUT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A Korean market holiday for presidential elections thinned\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regional trade, and the Taiwan dollar was spared further\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fallout from Wednesday's ratings downgrade by suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar stayed in a 1.7460-1.7470 range most\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the day, after some morning covering of short U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions and fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  saw it ease from an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore high of 1.7445 per dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It struck a 3-= month high of 1.7420 this week, sparking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par concern that it may overshoot the trade-weighted band it is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par managed in, which could prompt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strength.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Thai baht was lethargic around Wednesday's five-week\par highs just under 43 per dollar.\par     The Taiwan dollar slipped early to a two-week low of 34.897\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par per dollar, extending Wednesday's decline after Standard &\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Poor's downgraded the country's rating, before recovering to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 34.85 on suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, it could not firm past 34.85.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par News of the large equity raising by PT Astra International\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par could not help the Indonesian rupiah back towards the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par four-month highs around 8,800 it set earlier in the week, even\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par though it is expected to attract some foreign inflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par This week, Singapore's Cycle & Carriage Ltd committed up to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $87.5 million to subscribe for the rights issue planned to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par raise about $160 million.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0800 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 