\par\par \b \uc2  US Dlr Falls To S$1.7449 On Singapore Trade Data \b0\par\par\uc2 387 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2002\par 05:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The U.S. dollar weakened against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , falling to levels not seen since since July 25, after a government report showed the island republic's trade performance in November far exceeded economists' expectations. \par \par \uc2  At 0502 GMT, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7430, sharply down from S$1.7462 immediately before the trade report was issued. \par \par \uc2  International Enterprise Singapore said non-oil domestic exports rose 19% on year to S$9.5 billion in November. The faster growth follows a 5.7% rise in October and tops the average forecast of 8.2% expansion by 10 economists surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires. Individual forecasts ranged between a 6.5% and 10% expansion. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's stronger-than-expected trade data were a huge relief for investors as the numbers suggest fourth-quarter gross domestic product might be given the boost it needs to see the city-state avoid a double-dip recession, economists said. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's GDP grew 3.9% on year in the third quarter but fell a seasonally-adjusted, annualized, quarter-on-quarter 10.1%. A second consecutive quarter-on-quarter contraction would push the economy into its second recession in a year. \par \par \uc2  While the trade data were the main factor that lifted the Singapore dollar earlier, traders also attributed the U.S. dollar's fall to its weakness against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Traders also said that the local dollar's sharp strengthening against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to trigger any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the island's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Compared with other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Singapore dollar still looks weak on a trade-weighted basis, said a trader at an Asian bank here. \par \par \uc2  Using the exchange rate as its primary monetary policy tool, the MAS manages the value of the Singapore dollar against an undisclosed trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Some U.S.-dollar sell orders trickled into the market after the U.S. unit slipped below support at S$1.7460, with the trade data accelerating the decline, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar now has support at S$1.7430, then S$1.7400, they added. \par \par \uc2  -By Shen Hong, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4156; hong.shen@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020021217dych0008k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
