\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Singapore dlr hit 3-month highs. \b0\par\par\uc2 794 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2002\par 09:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Dec 17 (Reuters) - A unexpectedly strong rise in\par exports sent the Singapore dollar to its highest levels in over\par three months on Tuesday, as most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were lifted\par off their early lows by a rebounding yen.\par     The Singapore dollar rose to 1.7430 per dollar, last traded\par on September 5, from an early low of 1.7493, after data showed\par non-oil domestic exports had risen by 19 percent in November\par from a year earlier, more than double the average market\par forecast.\par     Dealers said a sharp rise had been expected to follow the\par hit exports took in October due to a lockout in U.S. West Coast\par ports. The exports data followed Monday's unexpected rise in\par October retail sales, which were up 1.8 percent on the year.\par     Analysts said the upbeat data would support the Sing dollar\par as it would douse expectations of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  shifting to\par an easing stance in its monetary policy review in January.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Not even a small portion of the market is worried about a\par widening (policy) band or a downright easing shift. Seems like\par they are taking comfort in the numbers," said Bhanu Baweja,\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS Warburg in Singapore.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore (MAS) manages the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against an undisclosed trade-weighted basket of which\par dollar, yen and euro are major components.\par     In October 2001, the MAS widened its policy band to allow\par larger exchange rate moves but said it would not seek an\par appreciation of the Sing dollar on a trade weighted basis.\par     Analysts believe the dollar's decline against the yen and\par euro this year may have taken quite a bit of pressure off the\par trade-weighted value of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar, and that is why\par the MAS has not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap the nominal exchange rate\par gains.\par  \par     "The Sing dollar hasn't gone beyond the band, it's still\par about 0.4 percent from the stronger end," Baweja said.\par     However, some dealers said the day's move was exacerbated\par by the thin year-end conditions.\par     BAHT, PESO OFF LOWS\par     Elsewhere, the Thai baht also recovered from early softness\par to test back towards 43.02 in late trade, a one-month high hit\par in New York on Monday.\par     Dealers in Bangkok said the baht was helped off it lows\par around 43.20 as the moves in the yen and Singapore dollar\par resulted in heavy dollar sales from foreign banks.\par     The Philippine peso hit a three-week low of 53.75 in early\par trade, and the beleaguered \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  proved unable to sustain\par slight gains and weakened into the close.\par     Dealers in Manila said a slowdown in dollar purchases from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local corporates and non-deliverable forward players helped the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par peso after its opening losses, but sentiment was depressed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after a government source told Reuters the January-November\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par budget deficit was likely to be around 200 billion pesos.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Manila's inability to arrest a gapping budget deficit, now\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forecast to hit 5.6 percent of gross domestic product this\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year, has dented investor confidence. The peso is Asia's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weakest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the dollar this year, losing over four\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The region's strongest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 2002, the Indonesian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rupiah, eased to back over 8,855 per dollar after it had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reached a three-month high of 8,805 on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Jakarta said local players choose to book\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par profits on the rupiah's recent gains before any further\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par appreciation on the back of expected dollar inflows from state\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par asset sales.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The South Korean won hit its strongest since September 9,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par encouraged by the yen's rebound. A finance ministry official\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par told Reuters the government was monitoring the rise of the won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closely.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar was off its early lows but worries over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outflows of foreign investment from local stocks capped its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0814 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.63       120.49         -0.12\par  Sing dlr      1.7434       1.7473         +0.22\par  Taiwan dlr    34.785       34.796         +0.03\par  Korean won   1195.80      1203.10         +0.61\par  Baht           43.03        43.09         +0.14\par  Peso           53.72        53.66         -0.11\par  Rupiah       8860.00      8805.00         -0.62\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.63       131.24         +8.80\par  Sing dlr      1.7434       1.8515         +6.20\par  Taiwan dlr    34.785       34.986         +0.58\par  Korean won   1195.80      1277.00         +6.79\par  Baht           43.03        44.16         +2.63\par  Peso           53.72        51.50         -4.13\par  Rupiah       8860.00     10350.00        +16.82.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021217dych00go6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
