\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Eye cenbanks, rupiah tests 8,800/dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2 865 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2002\par 05:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Dec 16 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah\par hit three-month highs on Monday as a weaker U.S. dollar lifted\par most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , although the rapid gains raised\par speculation that regional central banks may try to cap the\par rises.\par     The Singapore dollar was just off the three-month highs and\par the Thai baht  neared one-month highs, supported by the\par yen's  gains to around 120.5 per dollar, but traders said\par further sharp rallies were unlikely as central banks were\par expected to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  competitive.\par     "With the dollar likely to see trend weakness in the coming\par months, there certainly will be pressure on the Asian regionals\par to appreciate," said Bhanu Baweja, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS\par Warburg in Singapore.\par     He said better than expected economic numbers and recent\par investment inflows in equity markets had also helped sentiment\par in the regionals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But with the economic outlook clouded by a lacklustre\par recovery in the United States, export-driven Asia's single\par largest market, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength would be under the close\par watch of the region's central banks.\par     "Having already allowed the Asian regionals to appreciate\par strongly, Asian central banks would be weary of losing further\par competitiveness in their export markets," Baweja said.\par     Underscoring Baweja's view, the Singapore dollar stepped\par slightly away from its three-month highs hit on Friday as\par players speculated on possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par  \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        was around 1.7475 per dollar,\par from 1.7743 in New York on Friday, last traded on September 6.\par     Dealer said early U.S. dollar bids around 1.7450, on fears\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , prompted players to book profits\par on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar's recent gains.\par     Dealers said any impact from October's retail sales data\par due at 0500 GMT and exports data on Tuesday was likely to be\par moderate as weaker numbers have already been priced in.\par     Players were likely to stay cautious as thin year-end\par conditions could exacerbate price action, they said.\par     RUPIAH RISES, BAHT STEADY\par     The Indonesian rupiah rose to around 8,810 per dollar, its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par highest since September 9, supported by Sunday's part sale of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the country's leading overseas call operator, PT Indosat\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (ISAT.JK). Singapore's ST Telemedia won the bid for a 42\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent stake in the state-run telecom, agreeing to pay $634\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said the market was now likely to aim\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at 8,800, although thin flows from exporters and corporates\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would make players reluctant to take aggressive positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah is Asia's best performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 2002,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rising over 17 percent against the dollar, backed by steady\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows from sale of state assets and repatriation of earnings\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from exports due to higher yields at home.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Thai baht        traded around 43.24, after reaching a\par one-month high of 43.20 in offshore trade on Friday.\par     Sentiment was supported by the fast pace of gross domestic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par product growth in the third quarter. The state-run National\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Economic and Social Development Board said the economy grew 1.0\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in the third quarter, down from a 1.8 percent rise in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the previous three months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, third quarter GDP rose 5.8 percent over the year,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par faster than the 5.6 percent growth forecast by analysts and the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 5.1 percent year-on-year growth in the second quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The agency also said Thailand's economy would grow by 4.9\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent this year, beating analysts' expectations, and by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 3.5-4.5 percent in 2003.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bucking the regional trend, the friendless Philippine peso\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   eased to around 53.60 per dollar as demand for dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from the non-deliverable forwards market outpaced the supply\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from overseas workers repatriating earnings.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Manila said the peso could ease further as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows local corporates were hedging for a weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the start of next year and exporters were holding onto their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The South Korean won         gapped up with the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen, rising past 1,200 per dollar to its strongest since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par November 11. For a detailed report,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar  was around its highest since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par November 19, led by the yen, but talk of possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slowed its gains. For a detailed report, click on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par .\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0313 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.60       121.74         +0.95\par  Sing dlr      1.7475       1.7489         +0.08\par  Taiwan dlr    34.765       34.835         +0.20\par  Korean won   1201.10      1210.00         +0.74\par  Baht           43.22        43.29         +0.16\par  Peso           53.62        53.55         -0.13\par  Rupiah       8805.00      8870.00         +0.74\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.60       131.24         +8.82\par  Sing dlr      1.7475       1.8515         +5.95\par  Taiwan dlr    34.765       34.986         +0.64\par  Korean won   1201.10      1277.00         +6.32\par  Baht           43.22        44.16         +2.17\par  Peso           53.62        51.50         -3.95\par  Rupiah       8805.00     10350.00        +17.55.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216dycg0086j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\sh