\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Singapore dlr test highs, rest sit tight. \b0\par\par\uc2 516 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2002\par 09:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     SINGAPORE, Nov 29 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar\par tested two-week highs on Friday as thin trade kept most Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  within tight and familiar ranges.\par     Dealers said Thanksgiving holidays in the United States and\par waning corporate activity in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market ahead of the\par year-end have pushed trading volumes down.\par     "Market participants are reluctant to hold large positions\par heading into the year-end," said Thio Chin Loo, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par analyst at BNP Paribas in Singapore.\par     Earlier, the Singapore dollar touched 1.7616 per dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  just shy of 1.7602 hit overnight, before rolling back to around \par \par \uc2  1.7640 later in the day. The Singapore dollar has not breached \par \par \uc2  the 1.7600 level since November 15. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said while the risk of a corrective weakening in \par \par \uc2  the dollar against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  may increase the \par \par \uc2  demand for the Singapore dollar, its upside would be limited. \par \par \uc2  "Limiting any sharp appreciation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar \par \par \uc2  will be potential capital flight and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar competitive," Thio Chin Loo said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     She said that should keep the Singapore dollar within a\par 1.7560-1.7760 range until year-end.\par     Most analysts believe the recent strengthening of the\par Singapore dollar has pushed it closer to the stronger end of\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's undeclared policy band.\par     The Thai baht        was stuck in a tight 43.38-43.41\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range, against late Thursday's 43.36, in thin trading, as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar sales from foreign banks spotted in recent sessions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par faded away.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Dealers in Singapore said most local players kept to the\par sidelines or squared their positions ahead of the weekend.\par     The Philippine peso        stayed within its\par three-session-old 53.55-53.60 range amid fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at around 53.60 per dollar.\par     The Indonesian rupiah        was just below the 9,000 per\par dollar level, aided by dollar sales from state banks and waning\par demand from local corporates.\par     The Korean won            was easier but aided by\par equity-related inflows on the downside. For a detailed report,\par  \par     The Taiwan dollar            was slightly lower, reflecting\par the yen's  losses against the dollar. For a detailed\par report,\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.       $0803 GMT\par  Change on the day\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     122.43       122.21         -0.18\par  Sing dlr      1.7623       1.7661         +0.22\par  Taiwan dlr    34.812       34.805         -0.02\par  Korean won   1208.70      1207.80         -0.07\par  Baht           43.41        43.36         -0.12\par  Peso           53.53        53.59         +0.11\par  Rupiah       8971.00      8979.00