\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  talk aids peso as GDP slows. \b0\par\par\uc2 769 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 2002\par 05:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Nov 28 (Reuters) - Sentiment on the bewildered\par Philippine peso took another hit on Thursday after third\par quarter economic growth data came below expectations, although\par worries of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stopped it from falling.\par  \par     Elsewhere, Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were a touch firmer in subdued\par trade going into the U.S Thanksgiving holiday.\par     The Philippine economy grew 3.8 percent year-on-year in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  third quarter, down from 4.5 percent in the second quarter, as \par \par \uc2  a jump in manufacturing and services was held in check by flat \par \par \uc2  farm output. On a quarterly basis, the economy contracted 0.1 \par \par \uc2  percent. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     A Reuters poll of 10 economists had yielded an average\par forecast of 4.0 percent year-on-year growth.\par     Still, the peso held a tight 53.55-53.60 per dollar range,\par clear of Monday's 16-month low of 53.86, thanks to talk of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar sales, dealers in Manila said.\par     "The market is looking to bid up the dollar but with the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market players also know their\par limitations," said a dealer at a local bank in Manila.\par     He said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold about $5 million defending\par 53.60 per dollar, where the local market closed on Wednesday.\par     "Basically, a token \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through some foreign banks\par to tell the market that it does not want the peso to weaken\par further," the dealer said.\par     Dealers suspect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been in the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over the last week as since worries over a growing budget\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deficit and slowing growth knocked the peso to its 16-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lows. On Monday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  denied it had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some support for the peso was also expected after the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government said on Wednesday that it would issue up to five\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion pesos of dollar-linked three-year notes next week to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par juggle its budget deficit financing requirements for the year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were quiet, and a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lack of trading interest ahead of U.S. Thanksgiving holidays\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was likely to keep their upsides capped.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "In the previous two, three days, we already had a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par substantial amount of pre-holiday position squaring and now\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par people are not prepared to take substantial positions," said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Simon Flint, Bank of America's senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "In fact a lot of people would be rolling back risk\par progressively as the new year approaches," he added.\par     Flint said there was little impact on regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par from the dollar and Wall Street's rally after U.S. data raised\par hopes that the economy may be emerging from a weak spot.\par     BAHT STEADY\par     The Thai baht        was steady at around 43.42 per dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and recent equity sales by foreign investors was likely to keep\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it weighed down. The baht has spent the past two weeks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par contained in a 43.25 to 43.55 range\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Naomi Fink, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS Warburg, said the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par baht's upside was capped by dollar bids rumoured to be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par originating from telecom companies paying off some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar-denominated debt.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar held a narrow 1.7651-1.7670\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range with its upside seen capped by a weaker tone in the yen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah was also within its recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 8,900-9,000 range, with talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  activity limiting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par any weakness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Korean won            was off Wednesday's two-week\par highs tracking the yen's losses. For a detailed report, click\par on       .\par     The Taiwan dollar            was slightly down from\par Wednesday's finish of the onshore market, in line with the\par weaker yen. For a detailed report,\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0320 GMT\par  C