\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Ratings hurt peso, stocks buoy won. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Vidya Ranganathan \par \uc2 819 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 November 2002\par 10:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Nov 25 (Reuters) - Talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  supported an unloved Philippine peso at 16-month lows on Monday, while the Korean won hitched on to a stock market rally to rise as the U.S. dollar stalled on another attempt to surge against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Ratings agency Fitch cut its sovereign ratings outlook for the Philippines to negative from stable, citing a loss fiscal credibility, and markets are worried that one of the major agencies will soon downgrade the country. \par \par \uc2  Traders said other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were flat to slightly lower as the yen bounced off a three-week low of 123.19. \par \par \uc2  But they expect the U.S. dollar to stay strong this week on hopes of better economic data and stock market gains, which will allow it to benefit from the uncertainty over Japan's banks and the euro zone's troubles with growth. \par \par \uc2  "As U.S. markets slow for the long Thanksgiving holiday weekend, focus should shift to Japan's banking problem and Europe's less sanguine economic outlook," DBS Bank said in its market commentary. \par \par \uc2  "Our assessment is that the dollar should continue to expand on recent gains this week against the yen and euro, as well as Asian exchange rates, especially the peso," it said. \par \par \uc2  The Korean won rallied to 1,211 on a surge in foreign portfolio investments and the rise in its stock market to a two-month high. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar slipped to over 1.77 per dollar early on, and then held a 1.7715-1.7721 range. Traders reported some light U.S. dollar bids from a local bank in the morning, followed by low trading volumes. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar closed weaker at 34.804 despite a rise in share prices, as markets fretted over the weekend resignations of pro-reform Minister of Finance Lee Yung-san and the Chairman of the Council of Agriculture. \par \par \uc2  Both the won and Taiwan dollar enjoyed relative strength against other regionals last week as their stock markets rallied on signs of a global recovery in the technology sector. \par \par \uc2  FOREIGN STOCK BUYING HELPS BAHT \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht stuck to the 43.35-43.40 range seen last week, even as its regional counterparts slid as foreigners turned buyers once again in its share market. \par \par \uc2  "Though dollar/baht was biased higher on the margin this morning, mostly in line with a higher dollar/yen from Friday's offshore session, the pair's gains were capped by continued good performance in the local stock markets," Bank of America said in its market commentary. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah closed almost steady around 8,973-8,978 as hopes of further IMF funding and fresh foreign investment towards loan sales by the Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency supported the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Heavy local dollar demand had seen it weaken past 9,000 late last week. \par \par \uc2  "The generally lower levels of risk-aversion in global markets is providing a conducive environment for higher-yielders like the rupiah," Bank of America said. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso closed at a 16-month low of 53.85 despite suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the sliding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in morning trade after the Fitch cut. \par \par \uc2  Markets have been worried that the widening budget deficit and downward revision in growth forecasts could lead to a sovereign rating downgrade. As well, traders reported heavy dollar purchases by a power firm. \par \par \uc2  The peso opened local trading at Friday's low of 53.85 and dipped to 53.86, its lowest since July 2001. Data on the local dealing system showed a high trading volume of $93.5 million on Monday morning, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected, although volumes halved in afternoon trade. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the government announced the budget deficit to October exceeded the full-year target, and it set a new target - its fourth for 2002 - of 5.6 percent of GDP, about 220 billion pesos. It also cut the 2003 GDP growth forecast to 4.2-5.2 percent from 5.0-5.5 percent. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0845 GMT Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen     122.64       122.72         +0.07\par   Sing dlr      1.7713       1.7690         -0.13\par   Korean won   1211.50      1211.90         +0.03\par   Baht           43.36        43.34         -0.05\par   Peso           53.82        53.82         +0.00\par   Rupiah       8975.00      9000.00         +0.28\par   Change on year\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par   Japan yen     122.64       131.24         +7.01\par   Sing dlr      1.7713       1.8515         +4.53\par   Korean won   1211.50      1277.00         +5.41\par   Baht           43.36        44.16         +1.85\par   Peso           53.82        51.50         -4.31\par   Rupiah       8975.00     10350.00        +15.32 ((Vidya\par  Ranganathan, Asia Treasury Desk (65) 6870-3090\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par email:vidya.ranganathan@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021125dybp00jr8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
