\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  suspected after Philippine peso slips. \b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 November 2002\par 07:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Nov 25 (Reuters) - Suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stemmed the peso's slide as it struck a fresh 16-month low following a rating outlook downgrade. \par \par \uc2  The peso dipped to 53.86 in morning deals and subsequently settled around Friday's low at 53.85, levels last seen in July 2001, amid heavy dollar bids. \par \par \uc2  "I believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold around 70-80 million dollars around 53.85," a Manila-based trader said. Other traders put the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around half that estimate. \par \par \uc2  Data on the local dealing system showing an unusually high \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading volume of $93.5 million on Monday morning, compared with Friday morning's $75.5 million, and at an average weighted rate of 53.843, supported the view that there had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the trader said. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso has been dogged by worries its widening budget deficit and downward revision in growth forecasts could lead to a sovereign rating downgrade. \par \par \uc2  Rating agency Fitch on Monday lowered its outlook for the Philippines to negative from stable. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the government said the budget deficit to October had exceeded the full-year target, and it set a new target - its fourth for 2002 - of 5.6 percent of GDP, about 220 billion pesos. It also cut the 2003 GDP growth forecast to 4.2-5.2 percent from 5.0-5.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  Fitch has a BB-plus long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating on the Philippines. The country is rated BB-plus by Standard & Poor's with a negative outlook and Ba1 by Moody's Investors Service with a stable outlook. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021125dybp00dqn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
