\par\par \b \uc2  Indonesian rupiah drops 3.6 pct,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  seen. \b0\par\par\uc2 252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2002\par 04:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Oct 14 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah extended losses to 3.6 percent on Monday, despite suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cushion the slide, in reaction to the blasts on the resort island of Bali, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At its weakest point, the rupiah hit 9,350 per dollar, a level last seen at the end of April. \par \par \uc2  The weekend blasts, which killed at least 183 people, drove the rupiah down to 9,250 initially from Friday's close of 9,005/9,015. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Indonesian authorities were seen to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the rupiah around 9,300 rupiah to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The market went short of dollars before the weekend and is still covering," a Jakarta-based dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said Indonesia's Bank Restructuring Agency may also have sold some of the dollars it has been raising from sale of banks' bad loans. \par \par \uc2  No one has claimed responsibility for the bombs late Saturday night on Bali. The explosions ripped through packed nightclubs, popular with foreign tourists. \par \par \uc2  Fingers have been pointed to Osama bin Laden's al Qaeda network, blamed by the U.S. for the September 11 attacks on the United States. \par \par \uc2  Other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also weakened on Monday, especially the Philippine peso , fearing a spillover of the violence into the Philippines. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was quoted up to 1.8020, a five-month low, before it recovered and the Thai baht was around 44, a level not seen since early February. \par \par \uc2 Dokumen