\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Bow to dollar strength. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 580 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2002\par 10:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Aug 23 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso traded at \par \par \uc2  its lowest level since late 2001, the Taiwan dollar hit a \par \par \uc2  10-week low, and the Korean won and Thai baht touched two-week \par \par \uc2  lows as Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ceded ground to a rallying dollar on \par \par \uc2  Friday. \par \par \uc2      "The market was taken off guard by the dollar strength \par \par \uc2  overnight," said Thio Chin Loo, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \par \par \uc2  BNP Paribas. The dollar hit two week highs against the yen \par \par \uc2   and euro as recovering U.S. stocks boosted the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Thio said market momentum was now in favour of the dollar \par \par \uc2  and it would be some time before Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  found a \par \par \uc2  floor.     Dealers said position squaring ahead of the weekend \par \par \uc2  helped most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  off their lows, while rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aided the Philippine peso and the Taiwan \par \par \uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2  The peso fell to an eight-month low of 52.37 per \par \par \uc2  dollar before steadying on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk, which was \par \par \uc2  denied by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \par \par \uc2  would do so only in case of extreme volatility in the market. \par \par \uc2      Governor Rafael Buenaventura said the decline was \par \par \uc2  temporary, reflecting weakness across the region and reinforced \par \par \uc2  by negative domestic news, including Thursday's beheading of \par \par \uc2  two Christian preachers in the country's south by Muslim \par \par \uc2  extremists. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said sentiment was bearish on worries over \par \par \uc2  the budget deficit - which exceeded its 2002 target after just \par \par \uc2  seven months - and players simply used the comments to book \par \par \uc2  profits. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar fell to a 10-week low of 34.16 per \par \par \uc2  dollar, before talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped it recover some \par \par \uc2  losses. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar briefly touched 1.7601 per dollar, its \par \par \uc2  weakest since August 13, as the dollar strengthened. But dollar \par \par \uc2  sales by local corporates saw it recover later to around \par \par \uc2  1.7565. \par \par \uc2      A 0.4 percent fall in the July consumer price index from a \par \par \uc2  year earlier drew a muted market response. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht        was around 42.28 per dollar, off an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par early two-week low of 42.41. Dealers in Singapore said lack of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local factors and illiquid conditions had limited the downside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Korean won        dropped to a two-week low of 1,204.8\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par before paring its losses. Dealers in Singapore said the won was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par supported by inflows from settlement of export deals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Indonesian rupiah        was down at 8,865 per dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from late Thursday's 8,845. It hit a one-week low, but found\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par support in news that the bank restructuring agency has sold\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $2.5 billion worth of non-performing loans.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. $0806 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     119.82       119.10         -0.60\par  Sing dlr      1.7556       1.7513         -0.24\par  Taiwan dlr    34.139       34.057         -0.24\par  Korean won   1202.50      1193.70         -0.73\par  Baht           42.26        42.14         -0.28\par  Peso           52.30        52.15         -0.28\par  Rupiah       8865.00      8845.00         -0.23\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.82       131.24         +9.53\par  Sing dlr      1.7556       1.8515         +5.46\par  Taiwan dlr    34.139       34.986         +2.48\par  Korean won   1202.50      1277.00         +6.20\par  Baht           42.26        44.16         +4.50\par  Peso           52.30        51.50         -1.52\par  Rupiah       8865.00     10350.00        +16.75.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020823dy8n00ha9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
