\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - At multisession lows as dlr firms. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 689 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2002\par 04:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Aug 23 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were easier \par \par \uc2  in early Friday trade as the dollar rose to two week highs \par \par \uc2  against the yen and euro , with the Philippine \par \par \uc2  peso hitting an eight-month low after disappointing budget \par \par \uc2  deficit data. \par \par \uc2      The dollar was lifted by another day of gains on Wall \par \par \uc2  Street and signs of improvement in corporate bond markets \par \par \uc2  following a flood of corporate issuance, easing concerns that a \par \par \uc2  credit crunch might hurt capital spending and the economy. \par \par \uc2      "Near term, market action should remain dollar positive as \par \par \uc2  dictated by the consistency and strength of recent moves," said \par \par \uc2  Bhanu Baweja, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg. \par \par \uc2      "The developments, such as declining risk aversion and a \par \par \uc2  reviving corporate bond market, on which these moves are \par \par \uc2  predicated are fundamental in that they constitute the dollar's \par \par \uc2  key drivers and should be watched closely," he added. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippine peso        fell to an eight-month low of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 52.30 per dollar as sentiment was depressed by Thursday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par confirmation that the 2002 budget deficit target of 130 billion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pesos had been exceeded in just seven months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The January to July deficit was 133 billion pesos, but the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government said it would stick with its full year forecast.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Manila said the market was likely to target\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par one-year lows beyond 52.50, but wariness over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overbought signals on the dollar was deterring players from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par being too aggressive.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Charts showed the dollar/peso 14-day relative strength\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par index reading at 82.73, highlighting the risk of a correction\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the dollars' strength against the peso.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar fell to a 10-week low of 34.16 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, before bouncing back to 34.13 on talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        slipped about half a percent to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par test the 1.7600 level, last touched on August 13.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said some profit-taking in dollars, spotted around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.7590-1.7601 range, was pushing it back towards 1.7585, but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strong offers are not expected before 1.7635, the August 13\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par low.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The July consumer price index is expected at 0500 GMT, but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers said the focus would stay on the yen and euro - both\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par major components of the trade-weighted basket authorities in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore use to manage their exchange rate policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht        eased to 42.32 per dollar, from late\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday's 42.14, tracking losses in yen and other regionals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore said lack of local cues and illiquid\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par conditions were likely to keep the baht around 42.30-42.45.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Indonesian rupiah        was down at 8,865 per dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from late Thursday's 8,845, although it drew support from news\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the bank restructuring agency has sold $2.5 billion worth of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par non-performing loans.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Korean won            eased past the 1,200 per dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level, not seen since August 13, to touch a low of 1,204.8.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore said weak yen and wariness over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par equity-related outflows after recent sale of local stocks by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign funds was weighing down the won. But inflows from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par export deal settlements were expected to limit the losses.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.       $0223 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.10       119.10         -0.83\par  Sing dlr      1.7575       1.7513         -0.35\par  Taiwan dlr    34.120       34.057         -0.18\par  Korean won   1203.50      1193.70         -0.81\par  Baht           42.34        42.14         -0.47\par  Peso           52.21        52.15         -0.11\par  Rupiah       8860.00      8845.00         -0.17\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on 