\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Easier as dollar climbs on Wall St rise. \b0\par\par\uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 2002\par 05:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Aug 22 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were easier \par \par \uc2  in opening Thursday trade, taking their taking cue from a \par \par \uc2  weaker yen which slipped back over 119 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the dollar was drawing support from \par \par \uc2  stabilising U.S. stocks markets, after their rollercoaster \par \par \uc2  performance in past few weeks had raised global risk \par \par \uc2  perceptions. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, speeches by three U.S. Federal Reserve regional \par \par \uc2  presidents were seen as suggesting the economic recovery was on \par \par \uc2  track and there may not be need to cut interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "That rang a positive note to the ears of stock investors, \par \par \uc2  who seemed somewhat reassured by recovery hopes, sending stocks \par \par \uc2  rallying and thus providing support for the dollar," said Naomi \par \par \uc2  Fink, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Nasdaq Composite Index         rose 2.37 percent and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Dow Jones industrial average ended up 0.96 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     J.P. Morgan Chase in a research note said the near-term\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar rally would put most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  under pressure,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par particularly the Singapore dollar, South Korean won and Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, which are seen as more sensitive to moves in yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Against this, there could be some support for regionals if\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asian stocks follow Wall Street's lead\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar        touched a low of 1.7514 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar early on before dollar sales from foreign names pushed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it back to around 1.7480, still down from late Wednesday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.7472.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said with speculative positions mostly liquidated\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and given the lack of local leads, players were looking at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par capital flows for trading cues.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A tight trading range was expected with dollar bids spotted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at around 1.7465 and talk of dollar offers around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.7510-1.7520.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Korean won was easier at around 1,194.0 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, from Wednesday's onshore close of 1,192.0, as local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interbank players tracked the yen's lead.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Exporter dollar sales and equity-related inflows were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par protecting the downside, while second quarter gross domestic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par product had little impact on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par South Korea's Q2 GDP grew 1.4 percent from the previous\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quarter and was 6.3 percent higher than the same quarter a year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par earlier - almost in line with the 6.4 percent forecast in a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters survey of 10 economists.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar eased to around 34.04 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, after touching a low of 34.065, against Wednesday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par onshore close of 33.995.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Tuesday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , suggesting authorities were in not\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in favour of any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength at this moment, would keep\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exporters cautious.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht        was down by about a quarter of a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent from late Wednesday's 42.04 per dollar in thin trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The bearish regional tone weighed down the baht, but dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sales by exporters and foreign names, and a reluctance to take\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par significant positions due to lack of liquidity was seen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par limiting the baht's downside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso eased beyond 52 per dollar on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par low volumes as the market awaited budget deficit data now\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected later in the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah eased to 8,845 per dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from late Wednesday's 8,825, on dollar purchases from local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporates and foreign banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020822dy8m006hd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
