\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Reined in by Taiwan independence talk. \b0\par\par\uc2 705 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2002\par 05:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Aug 5 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped on \par \par \uc2  Monday morning as Taiwan's talk of independence from China and \par \par \uc2  more worries about the impact of a slower U.S economy on the \par \par \uc2  region's export-reliant countries turned the market jittery. \par \par \uc2      Taiwan President Chen Shui-bian's controversial remarks \par \par \uc2  that Taiwan and China were really separate countries knocked \par \par \uc2  the Taiwan dollar and the TAIEX share index in \par \par \uc2  early trade, drawing more attention than the U.S. economic \par \par \uc2  troubles. \par \par \uc2      A second factor weighing down \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the Japanese \par \par \uc2  yen's failure to make significant headway against the \par \par \uc2  dollar, despite depressing U.S. manufacturing and employment \par \par \uc2  data and falling stocks, as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders waited for Japan \par \par \uc2  to release its leading economic index later in the day. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar       , Philippine peso         and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan dollar erased early gains, while other\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regionals were mostly steady.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Talk about the Taiwan independence comments and the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par possibility of negative reaction from China is weighing on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Peter Redward, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Deutsche Bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Taiwan's Chen told a gathering of pro-independence\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par activists in Tokyo during a video conference on Saturday that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par he supported legislation for a referendum, a move certain to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par anger Beijing.     Redward said those tensions would keep\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwanese assets under pressure, but regional impact would be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par limited unless there was military action by China.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar fell to 33.80/90 per U.S. dollar from a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close of 33.72, supported lightly by hopes authorities would\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cushion sharp moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar failed to hold on to brief gains above\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.75 in the morning on concerns it was getting too close to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par being overvalued in trade-weighted terms.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts say Singapore's highly export-dependent economy is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par most at risk within the region if growth in the United States,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asia's biggest export market, slides further.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Indonesian rupiah        was steady around its previous\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 9,075/85, but traders expected it to lose ground to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the dollar since it had failed to respond to a run of positive\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par news, gaining just 0.6 percent last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Indonesia's Bank Restructuring Agency has recently managed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to sell non-performing loans, some to foreigners. As well, PT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Telekomunikasi Indonesia closed a deal to sell a cellular unit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to Singapore's SingTel for $429 million.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The telecom sale, the loans auction and falling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflation...none of that has been reflected in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves. Besides, Jakarta equities remain under\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pressure," Redward said, adding he expected to see the rupiah\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weaken towards 9,500 per dollar soon.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thailand baht        was steady, hugging the 42 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar level, barely changed from Friday's close at 42.10 and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pinned down by fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Last week, Thai Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reprimanded the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for letting the baht swing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sharply.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippine peso        was marginally weaker at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 51.32/39 compared with Friday's 51.27 per dollar close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Korean won        was dragged down by weak stocks, to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par be at 1,186 from Friday's 1,184.3 per dollar, although traders\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said exporters had a bullish view on their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par eager to sell overseas earnings quickly.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0300 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     118.78       118.94         +0.13\par  Sing dlr      1.7525       1.7556         +0.18\par  Taiwan dlr    33.880       33.723         -0.46\par  Korean won   1186.00      1184.30         -0.14\par  Baht           42.05        42.10         +0.12\par  Peso           51.38        51.27         -0.20\par  Rupiah       9080.00      9080.00         +0.00\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.78       131.24        +10.49\par  Sing dlr      1.7525       1.8515         +5.65\par  Taiwan dlr    33.880       34.986         +3.26\par  Korean won   1186.00      1277.00         +7.67\par  Baht           42.05        44.16         +5.02\par  Peso           51.38        51.50         +0.24\par  Rupiah       9080.00     10350.00        +13.99\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020805dy85005eu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
