\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Weighed down by firmer dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2002\par 04:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, July 26 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost \par \par \uc2  further ground to a firmer dollar in early Friday trade though \par \par \uc2  reluctance to take aggressive positions ahead of the weekend \par \par \uc2  was likely to keep the downside limited, traders said. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said they expected cautious trading on uncertainty \par \par \uc2  over the near-term direction of the dollar/yen and \par \par \uc2  persistent dollar purchases from foreign funds seeking to cover \par \par \uc2  their stock losses in global equities. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar firmed to a session high of 117.50 yen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and edged up to $1.0028 against the euro .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets are likely to remain volatile in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short-term, pulled by forces of position liquidation versus the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fundamental underpinnings for a weak dollar," said Thio Chin\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Loo, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at BNP Paribas in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar briefly touched a session low\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 1.7465 per dollar, from late Thursday's 1.7426, on dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sales by some foreign names, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market will be watching June manufacturing data, due by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par midday, for clues to the pace of recovery, after June data for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par durable goods orders in the U.S. showed a 3.8 percent surprise\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fall, its steepest in seven months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A vital statistic on the demand conditions in Asia's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par largest market, also showed a 3.9 percent drop in demand for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par computers and electronic products.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The fall in U.S. orders also weighed down the Taiwan dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  which eased to 33.622 per dollar, its lowest in about\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a month, with added pressure from equity-related dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said the Taiwan dollar was likely to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stay depressed after Thursday's aggressive dollar-buying\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and weaker than expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quarterly profits by the world's largest contract chipmaker,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Co.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht        held a tight range around 41 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar as trade resumed after a public holiday on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said wariness over verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by authorities expressing aversion to a strong baht was likely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to keep the baht's upside capped, with dollar bids from U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par names expected at around 40.80 per dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dollar offers around the 41.20-41.30 range were likely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to limit the baht's downside too.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippine peso        fell to a three-week low of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 50.74, from Thursday's onshore close of 50.66, on rising dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par demand from local corporates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Indonesian rupiah        was expected to be supported\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by dollar sales from state banks just ahead of the 9,000 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Korean won         -2 was weighed down to 1,171.8 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, from Thursday's onshore close of 1,170.9, on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par equity-related dollar outflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore said dollar inflows from month-end\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par export deals settlements was expected to cap the won's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par downside, with talk of offers at around 1,175.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.       $0225 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     117.40       116.42         -0.83\par  Sing dlr      1.7506       1.7426         -0.46\par  Taiwan dlr    33.639       33.409         -0.68\par  Korean won   1181.60      1170.90         -0.91\par  Baht           41.23        41.05         -0.44\par  Peso           50.77        50.66         -0.21\par  Rupiah       8999.00      8995.00         -0.04\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.40       