\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Regionals volatile, yen slips off radar. \b0\par\par\uc2 688 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juli 2002\par 12:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, July 25 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  volatile on Thursday, as the dollar's renewed weakness, \par \par \uc2  uncertain foreign investment flows and the narrow movements of \par \par \uc2  the Japanese yen made trading indecisive. \par \par \uc2      The dollar fell across the board, even dipping below parity \par \par \uc2  against the euro , as concerns over the U.S. economy and \par \par \uc2  assets resurfaced even as stocks there rallied. \par \par \uc2      Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed initially and later see-sawed as \par \par \uc2  fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese monetary authorities limited \par \par \uc2  the yen's movements. \par \par \uc2      Traders said they expected the yen's movements to be \par \par \uc2  restricted in the days to come and Asia would be influenced to \par \par \uc2  a greater extent by equity market flows. \par \par \uc2      "To the extent that the yen is not expected to deviate much \par \par \uc2  from the current settings, equity flows will drive the Asian \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Jan Lee, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Hypo-und \par \par \uc2  Vereinsbank AG. \par \par \uc2      "We expect a multi-week equity markets consolidation and \par \par \uc2  Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be ranged for a week or so." \par \par \uc2      With expectations that the yen will strengthen \par \par \uc2  substantially quite low, traders said they anticipate very \par \par \uc2  little verbal or physical \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Asian central banks. \par \par \uc2      SING DOLLAR EDGES HIGHER \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar's        progress above the 1.74 level\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was fleeting. By the close, it had erased part of its gains and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was trading around 1.7430/40 per dollar, higher than\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday's 1.7451 finish.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Korean won -2 also could not hold on to its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par highs of around 1,166 per dollar. It slipped below 1,170 while\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading firmer than Wednesday's close of 1175.10.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won had been pressured by equity-related outflows in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent sessions but traders expect possible heavy inflows from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SK Telecom's overseas issue to provide support.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SK was expected to price its exchange bonds and American\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Depositary Receipts on Thursday and the markets are forecasting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows of about $1.7 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Trading in the Thai baht was thin due to a religious\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par holiday, restricting its gains to around 41 per dollar from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday's close of around 41.25.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Expectation of foreign inflows into Indonesia, part of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par nearly $2.5 billion the Indonesian Bank Restructuring Agency\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hopes to raise from a sale of non-performing loans, could not\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par drive the rupiah any higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah        traded most of the day at 8990/9010, just\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par marginally above the previous session's finish around 9035.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Friday's trading could be distracted by court proceedings,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as a much awaited judgement in the murder trial of former\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par president Suharto's son Tommy Suharto is due to be delivered.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders reported dollar purchases by onshore players to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fund corporates in the Philippines. Despite talk of foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows, the peso's gains were minimal. It was quoted at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 50.65/68 per dollar compared with the previous day's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 50.70.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar stayed weak, quoting around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 33.41 per dollar. Traders said suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb the Taiwan dollar's gains and some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par equity-related outflows pressured the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0915 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     116.42       117.31         +0.76\par  Sing dlr      1.7426       1.7451         +0.14\par  Taiwan dlr    33.409       33.437         +0.08\par  Korean won   1171.20      1175.10         +0.33\par  Baht           41.05        41.25         +0.49\par  Peso           50.65        50.70         +0.10\par  Rupiah       8995.00      9035.00         +0.44\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change 