\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Edging higher, but lacking solid leads. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 679 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 2002\par 05:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, July 18 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  edged \par \par \uc2  higher in early Thursday trade but did not stray too far from \par \par \uc2  their recent ranges because of a lack of fresh, strong leads. \par \par \uc2      The dollar's bounce off a 17-month low against the yen \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par        and a 2-=   year low against the euro        also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deterred regional players from building short dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Korean won         -2 took its cue from an easier yen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as trade resumed after a holiday on Wednesday, and fell to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 1,173 per dollar from the previous onshore close of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,171.8.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said wariness over repeated actual and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Korean authorities, as the won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par appreciated to a 20-month high of 1,169.5 on Tuesday, had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dampened demand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said talk in the market that authorities may continue\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to defend the dollar's decline beyond 1,170, and the yen's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par failure to appreciate beyond 115.50, could keep the won under\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pressure.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The neighbouring Taiwan dollar          held steady at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 33 per U.S. dollar, with traders uncertain if the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would allow further gains in face of an easier\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar strengthened on Wednesday to 32.876, its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strongest since May 2001. But was pushed back to the 33 level\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped in to buy dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said unless exporters, the main supplier of dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in recent sessions, return to the market the Taiwan dollar will\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tread in a tight range around the 33 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In Southeast Asia, the Singapore dollar        firmed to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 1.7360 per dollar, from 1.7398, as dollar offers just\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ahead of 1.7400 prompted players to beef up their short dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said a firmer tone in the Thai baht        and the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesian rupiah also turned sentiment in favour of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sing dollar after it hit a early low of 1.7395.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht        edged up to 40.45 per dollar, from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par late Wednesday's 40.47 and an early session low of 40.525, amid\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a lack of demand for dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore said while most were still looking to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sell dollars, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's announcement that it was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par putting the baht on a "managed float" has raised the prospect\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of more frequent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and doubts on the baht's upside\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par potential.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said late\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this week to curb\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market volatility and has put the baht on a "managed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par float" as it surged to near two-year highs around 40.20.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the market would be cautious of retesting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 40.20, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has twice \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  before there,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but they expected strong support around 40.80 to the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Indonesian rupiah        rose to 8,925, from late\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday's 8,950 per dollar, as players slashed long dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions in anticipation of inflows from recent sales of state\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par assets and on plans to sell non-performing loans worth over $16\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.       $0223 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     116.57       116.37         -0.17\par  Sing dlr      1.7366       1.7398         