\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Surrender gains on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 667 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2002\par 04:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , July 12 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed \par \par \uc2  off recent highs early on Friday as the yen retreated \par \par \uc2  from a fresh 10-month peak and South Korea threatened to buy \par \par \uc2  more dollars to rein in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Dealers said state-run Korean banks bought an estimated \par \par \uc2  $300 million on Thursday to pull the won -2 from a \par \par \uc2  fresh 20-month high of 1,171.5 versus the dollar. \par \par \uc2      That had raised fears central banks elsewhere, especially \par \par \uc2  those of export rivals Singapore and Taiwan, might not like to \par \par \uc2  see their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthen in the face of an easier won. \par \par \uc2      "Yen and won will be the greater factors today," said Naomi \par \par \uc2  Fink, UBS Warburg's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist in Singapore. \par \par \uc2      The Korean won dipped to a low of 1,186.9, from late \par \par \uc2  Thursday's 1,179.5, after a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  official at \par \par \uc2  the Finance Ministry said the won's steep rise was worrisome \par \par \uc2  and authorities would continue to take action if needed to \par \par \uc2  stabilise the market. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said given the bullrun in Korean equities \par \par \uc2  and a lack of confidence on the dollar's fate, the Korean \par \par \uc2  authorities face a tough challenge. \par \par \uc2  Equity-related inflows aided the Taiwan dollar in \par \par \uc2  not straying far from late Thursday's 33.284, but dealers in \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the market was cautious on fears of aggressive \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        was down at 1.7513, from late\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday's 1.7510 and 1.7460 in overnight London trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said interbank players continued to cover short\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar positions but some local corporates and foreign funds\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were spotted selling dollars ahead of 1.7534, the lowest level\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the session so far.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht eases to around 41.335 per dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from 41.15 late Thursday, before covering some of its losses\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par back to 41.21.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said offshore players were spotted buying dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par though local sentiment was supported by recent relaxed comments\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said late\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would allow baht to move with market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forces for now and monitor it closely before deciding its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Economic data also came positive with a consumer sentiment\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par survey showing confidence up for the ninth consecutive month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and June trade data showing third straight month of growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso briefly touched 50.45, its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lowest in the week, before recouping to around 50.40, still\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weak from Thursday's onshore close of 50.335.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said rising commercial demand and wariness over the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regional mood weighed down the peso.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, some cheer was due from Finance Secretary Jose\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Camacho's comments on a sharp improvement in revenue\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par collections for June.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Indonesian rupiah languished beyond the 9,000 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar level, about percent down at 9,170, from late Thursday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 9,050, reeling from corporate demand for the dollars to repay\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign debts.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.       $0207 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     116.94       117.45         +0.44\par  Sing dlr      1.7512       1.7510         -0.01\par  Taiwan dlr    33.287       33.284         -0.01\par  Korean won   1185.00      1179.50         -0.46\par  Baht           41.25        41.15         -0.24\par  Peso           50.43        50.34         -0.19\par  Rupiah       9140.00      9050.00         -0.98\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan 