\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Step back on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 742 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2002\par 11:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , July 11 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  down in late Thursday trade as players trimmed their short \par \par \uc2  dollar positions, fearing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities \par \par \uc2  to cap the yen's recent gains. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said with U.S. weekly jobless claims due later in \par \par \uc2  the day and the June retail sales numbers and University of \par \par \uc2  Michigan consumer sentiment survey on Friday, players who were \par \par \uc2  extremely short of dollars scrambled to cover those positions. \par \par \uc2      "The market finally decided to take a breather whether the \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  or not. They just wanted to \par \par \uc2  lighten up and start afresh," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2      He said a fresh round of verbal warnings by South Korean \par \par \uc2  authorities followed by dollar purchases by state banks and \par \par \uc2  with no surprises in Singapore's monetary policy review, \par \par \uc2  players saw no incentive to push regionals any higher. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said although the dollar, may get a brief reprieve, \par \par \uc2  risk-aversion in U.S. assets, with its bearish implications, \par \par \uc2  was very much intact. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar rose a quarter percent against the euro\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to around 98.62 cents and was steady versus the yen at 117.50\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at 0728 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar        fell to a session low of 1.7535\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par per dollar, from late Wednesday's 1.7490, after it failed to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par break 1.7480, its highest level of the day. It managed to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recover some losses and was around 1.7500 by 0808 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said interbank players and local corporates were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the main buyers of dollars. They said some foreign names were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par also seen covering their short dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Earlier in the day, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said it would maintain its stance of zero appreciation in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par nominal effective exchange rate for the second half of 2002 in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par view of a benign inflationary environment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The policy announcement follows Wednesday's surprisingly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strong second quarter gross domestic product growth data, which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par had pushed the Singapore dollar to a 9-=   month high of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.7457.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Korean won         -2 slipped to a session low of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,183.5, off a fresh 20-month high of 1,171.5. It took its cue\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from dollar sales by state-run banks after a barrage of verbal\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par warnings against the won's gain were made by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par finance officials, including Finance Minister Jeon Yun-churl.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Eyeing the onslaught by the Korean authorities, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in neighbouring Taiwan also stepped up its physical\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and weighed down its dollar to a low of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 33.29, from early high of 33.21.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, equity-related inflows and dollar sales by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exporters helped the Taiwan dollar end onshore trade at 33.284,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par compared to 33.282 on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht eased to a session low of 41.175, off\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par an early high of 41.08, as offshore players trimmed their short\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, the sentiment was supported by a consumer survey\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that showed confidence in June rose for the ninth straight\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par month after plunging in September in the wake of the attacks on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the United States.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso ended onshore trade at 50.33,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from a session high of 50.185, as interbank players followed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the regional tone and commercial dollar demand rose.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah eased to a five-week low of 9,040,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from around 8,900, as local corporates continued to buy dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for debt payment needs and some offshore players were also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par spotted cashing the greenback.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   