\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Touch fresh peaks but cautious. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 630 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2002\par 12:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, July 9 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held \par \par \uc2  their ground around multi-month highs in late Tuesday trade as \par \par \uc2  the dollar slipped to levels just shy of parity with the euro \par \par \uc2   and to a nine-month low against the yen . \par \par \uc2      Still dealers said with most players now short of dollars, \par \par \uc2  they were cautious over pushing regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  too far, \par \par \uc2  too soon amid fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by authorities. \par \par \uc2      "Though players are cautious, but a breach of last week's \par \par \uc2  lows (against the dollar) suggest they are ready to rebuild \par \par \uc2  short dollar positions," a senior dealer at a bank in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2      Japan's Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa stoked \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears by clarifying his weekend comments that had \par \par \uc2  tripped the dollar off a technical recovery. \par \par \uc2      Later a Korean finance ministry official expressed concerns \par \par \uc2  over the won's -2 rise to a 20-month high of 1,181.9 \par \par \uc2  and said the government would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever needed to \par \par \uc2  stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2      The Finance Ministry also said it would sell 500 billion \par \par \uc2  won in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  stabilisation bonds on July 10. \par \par \uc2      The won ended onshore trade at 1,182.2 per dollar, against \par \par \uc2  Monday's close of 1,191.40. Backed by a resilient economy and \par \par \uc2  foreign investment inflows, the won has gained slightly over \par \par \uc2  eight percent year to date. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar rose to 33.364 per dollar, a \par \par \uc2  level not seen since May 22, 2001, encouraged by the won's \par \par \uc2  performance and Monday's surprising rise in June trade numbers. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said a lack of aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen by the market as a signal that \par \par \uc2  authorities would tolerate \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength on the back of \par \par \uc2  improving economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's June exports rose 9.0 percent on the year, the \par \par \uc2  strongest in 16 months, while imports expanded at the fastest \par \par \uc2  pace in 19 months at 11.2 percent. \par \par \uc2  In the Southeast, the Thai baht rose to a 22-month high of \par \par \uc2  41.30 per dollar, on the back of dollar sales by exporters and \par \par \uc2  settlement of local stock purchases by foreign investors. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar breached the 1.7600 per dollar \par \par \uc2  level to touch a nine-month high of 1.7590, amid speculation \par \par \uc2  ahead of second quarter growth numbers, due on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso ended onshore trade at a \par \par \uc2  one-week high of 50.29, against its previous close of 50.47, \par \par \uc2  tracking other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a lack of dollar demand \par \par \uc2  from local corporates. \par \par \uc2  However, the Indonesian rupiah failed to sustain its gains \par \par \uc2  from opening levels this morning, despite the general bullish \par \par \uc2  regional tone. \par \par \uc2  Weighed down by local corporates' dollar purchases for debt \par \par \uc2  repayment needs, the rupiah languished around 8,900 levels, \par \par \uc2  against 8,890 in late Monday trade. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.       $0950 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     118.42       118.67         +0.21\par  Sing dlr      1.7596       1.7624         +0.16\par  Taiwan dlr    33.380       33.513         +0.40\par  Korean won   1182.20      1191.40         +0.78\par  Baht           41.27        41.41         +0.34\par  Peso           50.28        50.47         +0.38\par  Rupiah       8905.00      8890.00         -0.17\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.42       131.24        +10.83\par  Sing dlr      1.7596       1.8515         +5.22\par  Taiwan dlr    33.380       34.986         +4.81\par  Korean won   1182.20      1277.00         +8.02\par  Baht           41.27        44.16         +7.00\par  Peso           50.28        51.50         +2.43\par  Rupiah       8905.00     10350.00        +16.23\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020709dy7900kdh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
