\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Multi-month highs hit as dollar wobbles. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 770 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2002\par 05:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, July 9 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed \par \par \uc2  to multi-month highs early on Tuesday as the dollar, hobbled by \par \par \uc2  U.S. corporate accounting controversies, looked vulnerable to \par \par \uc2  further losses against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Dealers said with long dollar positions mostly wiped out on \par \par \uc2  Monday, most players in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were now looking to \par \par \uc2  position themselves short of dollars, showing a general lack of \par \par \uc2  confidence on the greenback. \par \par \uc2      "With the August 15 deadline for (U.S.) corporate \par \par \uc2  executives to vouch for the accuracy of their firms' financial \par \par \uc2  statements approaching, we expect further disclosures of \par \par \uc2  controversial accounting practices to dampen the outlook for \par \par \uc2  the dollar," said Naomi Fink, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS \par \par \uc2  Warburg in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wariness helped the dollar off a nine-month \par \par \uc2  low of 118.32 yen hit in early Sydney trade and stay \par \par \uc2  flat at 98.83/86 cents against the euro , but doubts \par \par \uc2  persisted. \par \par \uc2      Lee Boon Keng, treasury market strategist at DBS Bank, said \par \par \uc2  120 yen has become a new resistance level for the dollar \par \par \uc2  as Japan continues to pour out evidence of a cyclical recovery. \par \par \uc2      The latest number backing that view was Japan's machinery \par \par \uc2  orders for May released on Monday. A 0.2 percent on-the-month \par \par \uc2  rise surprised economists who had expected a 2.8 percent fall. \par \par \uc2      Surprising Taiwan trade data on Monday also reinforced the \par \par \uc2  view that recovery in other Asian economies was gaining \par \par \uc2  traction. \par \par \uc2      Taiwan's June exports rose 9.0 percent on the year, the \par \par \uc2  strongest in 16 months, while imports expanded at the fastest \par \par \uc2  pace in 19 months at 11.2 percent. \par \par \uc2      Responding to those numbers and to gains in the yen and \par \par \uc2  Korean won -2, the Taiwan dollar jumped to a \par \par \uc2  fresh 13-month high of 33.371 per dollar. \par \par \uc2      Dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped \par \par \uc2  the rise and pulled the Taiwan dollar back to around 33.395. \par \par \uc2  But dollar sales from exporters were expected to keep the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  supported, they added. \par \par \uc2      WON TESTS FRESH HIGHS \par \par \uc2      The Korean won, also backed by equity-related inflows, rose \par \par \uc2  to touch a high of 1,185.4, a level not seen since December 12, \par \par \uc2  2000. \par \par \uc2      Dealers in Singapore said exporters and offshore players \par \par \uc2  were selling dollars as foreign investors continued to buy \par \par \uc2  local stocks for the fourth consecutive session. \par \par \uc2      However, repeated verbal warnings by authorities \par \par \uc2  threatening action against excessive gains in the won kept \par \par \uc2  players cautious and capped further gains. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In the southeast, the Singapore dollar        breached the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.7600 per dollar level to touch a nine-month high of 1.7590.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said speculation of better-than-expected second\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quarter growth numbers, due on Wednesday, was fuelling the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rally. But with the market now short of dollars, gains were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected to be limited.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht touched a high of 41.35 per dollar, a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level not seen since September 12, 2000, as dollar sales by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore players gained momentum.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Bangkok said several U.S. and European banks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were spotted selling dollars, prompting local players to take\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fresh short dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, rumours of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar purchases were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected to keep the baht's gains limited from these levels.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippine peso        also gained in line with other\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , rising to a one-week high of 50.38 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, but talk of corporate dollar bids at 50.30-50.35 was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par likely to cap further gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The only detractor of the regional trend was the Indonesian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rupiah , which eased to around 8,900 from late Monday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 8,890 on dollar purchases by local corporates and state-run\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banks.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.       $0313 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     118.64       118.67         +0.03\par  Sing dlr      1.7598       1.7624         +0.15\par  Taiwan dlr    33.381       33.513         +0.40\par  Korean won   1188.00      1191.40         +0.29\par  Baht           41.40        41.41         +0.02\par  Peso           50.38        50.47         +0.18\par  Rupiah       8906.00      8890.00         -0.18\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.64       131.24        +10.62\par  Sing dlr      1.7598       1.8515         +5.21\par  Taiwan dlr    33.381       34.986         +4.81\par  Korean won   1188.00      1277.00         +7.49\par  Baht           41.40        44.16         +6.67\par  Peso           50.38        51.50         +2.22\par  Rupiah       8906.00     10350.00        +16.21\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020709dy790066d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
