\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Firmer on weak dollar, won shines. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 782 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 2002\par 12:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, July 8 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  firmer in late Monday trade following news of more inflated \par \par \uc2  accounting at U.S. firms and on a surprising lack of dollar \par \par \uc2  support in fresh comments by Japan's finance minister. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said most players opted to bail out of long dollar \par \par \uc2  positions they had taken in response to last week's upward \par \par \uc2  correction in the greenback against the yen and euro \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2      That and signs of renewed interest among foreign investors \par \par \uc2  in local stocks helped the Korean won -2 strengthen to \par \par \uc2  a fresh 19-month peak and the Singapore dollar and Thai \par \par \uc2  baht to one-week highs. \par \par \uc2      "All eyes are now fixed on whether the dollar/yen breaches \par \par \uc2  its June 28 low (of 118.30) which will trigger a fresh round of \par \par \uc2  dollar sales," said a senior dealer at a European bank in \par \par \uc2  Singapore. \par \par \uc2      Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa's comment on the weekend \par \par \uc2  that world financial authorities believed a weakening of the \par \par \uc2  dollar was in progress pressured the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which Tokyo \par \par \uc2  itself had repeatedly propped up in the past several sessions. \par \par \uc2      Further weighing down the dollar was news late on Friday \par \par \uc2  that Houston-based energy firm Reliant Resources Inc \par \par \uc2  had erased $7.9 billion in revenues and the Wall Street Journal \par \par \uc2  Europe Monday report that drugs giant Merck & Co \par \par \uc2  recorded billions in revenue that were never collected. \par \par \uc2      WON BREACHES 1,200/DLR \par \par \uc2      The won breached 1,200 to levels not seen since December \par \par \uc2  17, 2000, largely ignoring the Finance Ministry's verbal \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and dollar sales by some state-run banks early in \par \par \uc2  the day. \par \par \uc2      A senior Finance Ministry official said authorities were \par \par \uc2  concerned about the impact of the won's appreciation on the \par \par \uc2  economy and exports and vowed to take active steps to stabilise \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2      Dealers in Singapore said offshore players sold dollars \par \par \uc2  encouraged by the third consecutive session of local stock \par \par \uc2  buying by foreign investors. \par \par \uc2      The won touched a high of 1,191.2 per dollar, before easing \par \par \uc2  back slightly to 1,191.4 at the close of the onshore trade. \par \par \uc2  That was up 1.13 percent against Friday's close of 1,204.90. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said a test of higher levels around 1,180 was \par \par \uc2  expected in coming sessions though interbank players were \par \par \uc2  cautious on fears of the oft threatened physical \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  by authorities. \par \par \uc2      SING DLR, BAHT REGAIN PEAKS \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        strengthened by about half a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent to a one-week high at 1.7628 per dollar, against late\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday's 1.7720.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said dollar's decline versus the yen and euro and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par moderate dollar demand from local corporates sent interbank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players covering short Sing dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Talk of dollar bids around 1.7625, the Sing dollar's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par intraday  high of July 1, helped pull the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  back to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 1.7636.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said gains from these levels were likely to be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par limited ahead of second quarter economic growth estimates due\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Wednesday and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's mid-year policy review and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par macroeconomic analysis on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht        was at one-week highs around 41.40,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against late Friday's 41.62 on dollar sales by exporters and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore players.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Bangkok said dollar supply was mostly from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore and Hong Kong names.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Indonesian rupiah       , however, bucked the firmer\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regional trend, as some local names were spotted bidding\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars for corporate needs, pulling it down by about half a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent to 8,890, against late Friday's 8,845.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Jakarta said talk of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  selling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars to defend the 8,900 level, helped the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bounce\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par off an intraday low of 8,925.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     118.67       120.53         +1.57\par  Sing dlr      1.7624       1.7720         +0.54\par  Taiwan dlr    33.513       33.580         +0.20\par  Korean won   1191.40      1204.90         +1.13\par  Baht           41.41        41.62         +0.51\par  Peso           50.44        50.60         +0.31\par  Rupiah       8890.00      8845.00         -0.51\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7996         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.67       131.24        +10.59\par  Sing dlr      1.7624       1.8515         +5.06\par  Taiwan dlr    33.513       34.986         +4.40\par  Korean won   1191.40      1277.00         +7.18\par  Baht           41.41        44.16         +6.64\par  Peso           50.44        51.50         +2.10\par  Rupiah       8890.00     10350.00        +16.42\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020708dy7800l57\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
