\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -In cautious mood, but uptrend intact. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Anchalee Worrachate \par \uc2 692 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 2002\par 12:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , July 1 (Reuters) - Fears of Japan's \par \par \uc2  dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  held Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  back on \par \par \uc2  Monday, but their bullish tone was intact as the U.S. dollar \par \par \uc2  faced unrelenting pressure over disillusionment with U.S. asset \par \par \uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2      Trading volumes were thin as several centres -- South \par \par \uc2  Korea, Thailand and Hong Kong -- were closed on holiday. They \par \par \uc2  will resume trading on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2      Japan monetary authorities on Friday defended the dollar in \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, using the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  and the U.S. Federal Reserve as its agents in overseas markets. \par \par \uc2      Even the country's better-than-expected "tankan" corporate \par \par \uc2  sentiment survey report on Monday barely lifted the yen. \par \par \uc2      At 0935 GMT, the dollar traded around 119.85 yen and \par \par \uc2  $0.9912 to the euro . \par \par \uc2      Despite the U.S. unit's pull back here and there, the \par \par \uc2  market  still favoured the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with most \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists keeping their long Asia/dollar positions. \par \par \uc2      "I can see the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  continue to appreciate in \par \par \uc2  the next nine to 12 months," said P.K. Basu, regional \par \par \uc2  strategist at Credit Suisse First Boston in Singapore, adding \par \par \uc2  he did not expect this round of the dollar's decline to hurt \par \par \uc2  export-dependent Asia. \par \par \uc2  "Given the fact that inflation is very tame across Asia, \par \par \uc2  the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are still pretty cheap on a real \par \par \uc2  effective basis," he said. \par \par \uc2  "Asia's exports are benefitting from recovery in global \par \par \uc2  demand. And since Asian countries primarily compete with one \par \par \uc2  another, the fact they are all appreciating together doesn't \par \par \uc2  really hurt any single exporter," he said. \par \par \uc2  SING $ RETREATS \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar stepped back, shedding around a \par \par \uc2  quarter of a percent on the back of the yen's losses. It was \par \par \uc2  trading at around 1.7663 to the dollar in late trade. \par \par \uc2      But its firm tone remained in place, with recent economic \par \par \uc2  data pointing to gradual but solid recovery. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht        was flat in the offshore market,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par giving up its earlier gains in sympathy with most other\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But it is still trapped in the uptrend channel against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. dollar. Charts shows the baht is being overbought,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par suggesting further upward moves could encounter some profit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par taking.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PESO EYES BUDGET\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso ended slightly weaker at 50.43 compared with 50.42\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the previous session, with the market focusing on fiscal\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par data due out later this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We advise investors to brace for a poor outturn," said a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Salomon Smith Barney report. "The deficit for the first five\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par months of the year will likely breach the 100 billion peso\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deficit mark, or less than 30 billion shy of the full-year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par target with seven months still to go."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  managed to clamber off its intraday lows of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 50.53, drawing mild support from news that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par successfully raised $675 million from five-year syndicated loan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par facility as the loan will lengthen the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par debt maturity profile.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar came off, ending its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par eight-session appreciation streak due to hefty local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ended at 33.568 to the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par compared with 33.560 at the open and 33.558 at the close on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0746 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     119.52       119.05         -0.39\par  Sing dlr      1.7656       1.7617         -0.22\par  Taiwan dlr   