\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals firm, WorldCom knocks dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Anchalee Worrachate \par \uc2 744 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2002\par 13:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, June 26 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were firmer \par \par \uc2  on Wednesday as the revelation about accounting irregularities \par \par \uc2  at the U.S. telecommunications giant WorldCom added to \par \par \uc2  the dollar's woes. \par \par \uc2      WorldCom said on Tuesday it had uncovered improper \par \par \uc2  accounting for almost $4 billion in expenses, marking the latest \par \par \uc2  case of accounting irregularities to hit U.S. companies. \par \par \uc2      The Bank of Japan has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in the market on \par \par \uc2  Wednesday to support the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with dealers estimating \par \par \uc2  it might have poured at least $4 billion into the market to slow \par \par \uc2  the yen's gains. \par \par \uc2      But the move did not do much for the dollar as concerns over \par \par \uc2  Corporate America -- confidence in which is crucial in \par \par \uc2  attracting inflows to finance U.S. gaping current account \par \par \uc2  deficit -- seemed to have taken the teeth out of the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      "There is a lot of bad news about U.S. companies. All in \par \par \uc2  all, it doesn't look pretty," said Claudio Piron, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  strategist at Standard Chartered in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      "In term of dollar yen, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this level is like \par \par \uc2  throwing your money away. You need the market to get short again \par \par \uc2  to have any real impact," he said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro        was edging closer to parity with the dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par surging to a 28-month high of $0.9941 earlier in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par session and was trading around $0.9925 by 1100 GMT. Against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen, the dollar was down one percent on the day at 119.60\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     WON AT FRESH 18-MONTH HIGH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Korean won         -2 closed at a fresh 18-month high on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the back of the dollar's weakness against the yen. The market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par appeared to have ignored the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's repeated jawboning\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against sharp won's appreciation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ended at 1,203.90 per dollar against 1,213.70\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at the close on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar          ended at a fresh 13-month high\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the dollar on the back of the yen and some exporter\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar offers ahead of the month-end.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It finished at 33.622 against Tuesday's 33.738. Dealers said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par they did not detect aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to slow\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SING $ ROBUST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar        was boosted by both the dollar's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weakness against the yen and better-than-expected May\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par manufacturing data.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The city-state's manufacturing production jumped 17 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on the year, thanks to strong growth in the biomedical sciences\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sector. The number far exceeded market expectations which ranged\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from around 3.0 percent contraction to 1.0 percent growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar rose to the intraday high of 1.7624 to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar -- its best level since early October last year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht        gained alongside other regionals,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading above 41.70. The market also took heart from positive\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local factors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Finance Ministry said on Wednesday that Thailand's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par public sector debt had declined to 53.53 percent of GDP at the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par end of March from 54.45 percent of GDP at end-February.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Exports grew for the second month in a row in May after 11\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par straight months of year-on-year declines.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippine peso        lagged others as the market was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par torn between gains in the regionals and caution caused by recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par financial jitters in Brazil.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The country is seen as a prime candidate in Asia for any\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par contagion affect from Latin America due to its weak fiscal\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par position and relatively high foreign debt.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  1026 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.11       121.65         +1.28\par  Sing dlr      1.7628       1.7708         +0.45\par  Taiwan dlr    33.622       33.738         +0.35\par  Korean won   1203.9       1213.70         +0.87\par  Baht           41.63        41.87         +0.59\par  Peso           50.35        50.45         +0.20\par  Rupiah       8670.00      8650.00         -0.23\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.11       131.24         +9.27\par  Sing dlr      1.7628       1.8515         +5.03\par  Taiwan dlr    33.622       32.900         -2.15\par  Korean won   1203.70      1277.00         +6.09\par  Baht           41.63        44.16         +6.09\par  Peso           50.35        51.50         +2.28\par  Rupiah       8670.00     10350.00        +19.38\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020626dy6q00mjd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
