\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Up Late; Hits 9-Mo High On US Dlr Weakness \b0\par\par\uc2 761 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2002\par 11:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar surged to a fresh nine-month high late Monday on the U.S. dollar's persistent weakness against its major counterparts and regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0855 GMT (4:55 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was at S$1.7656, down from S$1.7720 late Friday in Asia. It traded between S$1.7643 and S$1.7715. \par \par \uc2  In Asia Monday, the U.S. dollar opened weaker, extending the losses it suffered in New York late Friday, when it dropped below S$1.7700 amid more losses in the U.S. stock market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  broke immediate support at S$1.7685 in early Monday trading as local banks and U.S. investment houses kept up with their U.S. dollar sales. The outlook for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to worsen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  However, despite the U.S. dollar's sharp fall, market participants weren't too concerned that the move would draw the attention of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore, mainly because the U.S. dollar was broadly weaker against other Asian counterparts at the same time. \par \par \uc2  In a research report published Monday, United Overseas Bank said it doubts the MAS would be uncomfortable with the U.S. dollar's inherent weakness against the Singapore dollar and reckons the MAS' undisclosed lower limit for the U.S. dollar to have slipped to S$1.7500. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar at one point Monday bounced higher against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, albeit briefly, when Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen. The U.S. dollar shot up to Y122.76 from Y121.02. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar soon tumbled again against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the Singapore dollar, which touched a fresh nine-month low of S$1.7643, when Europe-based players joined in the U.S. dollar selling in favor of a strong euro late in the Asian trading day, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight, the U.S. dollar is expected to test lower, "unless they (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again," said a dealer at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  Barring that, the U.S. dollar may head toward its next support at S$1.7600. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds were mostly higher Monday, in tandem with gains in U.S. Treasurys late Friday, and as local interbank rates stayed weak, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Most tenors had started the local session higher and held up through the day, though volumes tapered off slightly, in the wake of the heavy flows seen last week, dealers added. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the political uncertainty in Malaysia following Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad's flip-flop over resigning dissipated early in the session. \par \par \uc2  Mahathir announced before a national television audience Saturday that he was quitting but changed his mind about an hour later after entreaties from leaders of United Malays National Organisation, or UMNO, the dominant political party in Malaysia's ruling coalition. Mahathir then left Sunday on a previously unannounced 10-day vacation. \par \par \uc2  The yield on two-year bonds ended five basis points lower at 1.39%, while the yield on five-year bonds fell 10 basis points to 2.66%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds fell nine basis point to 3.15% and the yield on 10-year bonds fell six basis points to 3.58%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds fell seven basis points to 3.95%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2  In the interest rate swaps market, swaps tracked local bond yields lower, with the most liquid seven-year swap offer falling eight basis points to 3.36% and the 10-year swap offer slipping six basis points to 3.71%. \par \par \uc2  The spread between two- and 10-year swaps widened to 201 basis points, from 200 basis points late Friday. \par \par \uc2  In the local money market, rates were mixed, though liquidity remained flush in the banking system. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Monday       Late Friday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.7500% 0.8750%   0.6875% 0.8125%\par 3-Month           0.7500% 0.8750%   0.7500% 0.8750%\par 1-Year            1.0000% 1.1250%   1.0625% 1.1250%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-64154-157;\par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020624dy6o000jr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
