\par\par \b \uc2  SGX Nikkei 225 Futures End Up; BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Lifts Mkt \b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2002\par 09:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- The Nikkei 225 stock index futures traded on the Singapore Exchange ended higher Monday, after the Bank of Japan entered the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb the U.S. dollar's slide against the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark Nikkei 225 September contract closed up 80 points at 10,400, with 15,624 contracts traded. \par \par \uc2  On the spot market, the Nikkei 225 rose 1.1% to 10,471.32 points. \par \par \uc2  The futures started the day with a bearish tone, tracking losses in U.S. stocks Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones Industrial Average fell 177.98 points to 9253.79, while the Nasdaq shed 23.79 points to 1440.96. \par \par \uc2  However, expectations for and then the actual presence of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market boosted sentiment among equities investors, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  As the BOJ bought dollars for yen, the fortunes of Japanese exporters also improved accordingly in the stock market. \par \par \uc2  At 0651 GMT (2:51 a.m. EDT), the dollar was quoted at Y121.74, above Y121.12 late Friday in New York, but still below Y123.36 late Friday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  A weaker yen against the dollar is often considered beneficial for Japan's export-oriented economy. \par \par \uc2  BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  triggered some short-covering in the futures market, dealers said, adding that if prices continue to rise, more short position holders will probably be forced to close their contracts. \par \par \uc2  Nikkei September now faces resistance at 10,550, with support at 10,000, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The MSCI Taiwan stock index futures traded in Singapore ended lower, with the benchmark June contract down 1.6 points at 239.9. \par \par \uc2  On the spot market, the benchmark index of the Taiwan Stock Exchange ended 75.64 points, or 1.4%, lower at 5384.89. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                         Monday    Previous   Change (Pts)\par Nikkei 225 Sep          10400     10320      up 80\par Nikkei 300 Sep          198.4     197.0      up 1.4\par Nikkei 225 Spot Index   10471.32  10354.35   up 116.97\par MSCI Taiwan Jun         239.9     241.5      dn 1.6\par Taiwan Weighted Index   5384.89   5460.53    dn 75.64\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Shen Hong, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4156;\par hong.shen@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1095 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020624dy6o000e8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
