\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Going strong as Mideast clouds dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Anchalee Worrachate \par \uc2 769 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2002\par 05:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, June 20 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept their \par \par \uc2  strength as more rumblings in the Middle East added woes to the \par \par \uc2  wobbly dollar, which was still languishing near its multi-month \par \par \uc2  lows against the euro and the Swiss franc . \par \par \uc2      The dollar sank anew after a Palestinian suicide bomber in \par \par \uc2  Jerusalem killed seven people and wounded about 35 at a bus \par \par \uc2  stop. News that the U.S. Secret Service briefly evacuated the \par \par \uc2  White House after an aircraft flew into restricted airspace a \par \par \uc2  few miles away from the president's residence also unsettled \par \par \uc2  the market. \par \par \uc2      Although the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed to recover some lost \par \par \uc2  ground after the White House scare cleared, it remained \par \par \uc2  vulnerable as investors still questioned the valuations of the \par \par \uc2  U.S. assets. \par \par \uc2      "Most of my clients almost universally take a bearish view \par \par \uc2  on the dollar and U.S. assets which, relative to other markets, \par \par \uc2  are still expensive," said a fund manager at one U.S. firm in \par \par \uc2  Singapore. \par \par \uc2      "U.S. companies will need strong growth to justify the \par \par \uc2  current prices. Although there is evidence the U.S. is \par \par \uc2  recovering, the quality of its growth is not going to be that \par \par \uc2  fantastic," he said. \par \par \uc2      Economists said Asia should benefit if investors shift \par \par \uc2  their investments from the United States to seek better \par \par \uc2  risk-adjusted returns. \par \par \uc2      "Perhaps the cash portions (of investments) have gone up \par \par \uc2  significantly, because apart from Thailand, we haven't seen \par \par \uc2  significant inflows into these markets for a while on a trend \par \par \uc2  basis," said James Malcolm, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan. \par \par \uc2      "This means there is probably some money waiting to come \par \par \uc2  into the rest of Asia in the second half of the year," he said. \par \par \uc2      THAI BAHT AWAITS NPL DATA \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht        extended gains, buoyed by a stream of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par capital inflows into local equities. But players appeared to be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reluctant to lift it past the 42 level. The baht was quoted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 42.08 per dollar at 0300 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been trapped in a protracted uptrend\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par channel against the dollar since early April on the back of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par improved sentiment toward cheap Thai assets and a shift in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market will be watching out for data on non-performing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par loans. After peaking at 47 percent of total loans in mid-1999,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thai non-performing loans now stand at around 10 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso was wedged in a tight range of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 50.140-50.270 to the dollar, with around $72.50 million traded\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par so far in the onshore market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Rafael Buenaventura's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par comments that the bank expected its key interest rates to be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par steady for the rest of the year barely moved the peso as it was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pretty much in line with market expectations.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The market is betting the U.S. Fed will keep its rates\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par anchored at 1.75 percent through year-end anyway. Given that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the fact inflation in the Philippines is pretty tame, we do\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expect the BSP to stay pat this year," said a Manila peso\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par WON, SING $ TRACK YEN\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Korean won -2 edged higher alongside the yen,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading near its intraday peak of 1,226.0 to the dollar. But\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its gains were dented by foreign investors' selling of local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar also followed the yen higher,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading around T$34.044 compared with 34.099 at the Wednesday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close. However, fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar-buying\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  limited its upside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar extended gains against the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after a stop was triggered overnight at around 1.7850.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was being quoted in a 1.7832-1.7860.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  023