\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Flat Late; Gives Up Gains As Bk Buy US Dlrs \b0\par\par\uc2 730 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 2002\par 12:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was lower against its U.S. counterpart late Friday, surrendering its early gains on U.S. dollar buying by banks amid \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears and to cover their short positions. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said, however, that volume was light and thin liquidity exaggerated the Singapore dollar's moves. \par \par \uc2  Around 0940 GMT (5:40 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7865, unchanged from Thursday in Asia. It traded between S$1.7835 and S$1.7892. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar opened lower at S$1.7845 in Asia, following its overnight decline against the yen and the euro, and fell in early trade on light follow through selling. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar hit an intraday low of S$1.7835 after Moody's Investors Service upgraded Singapore's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  country ceilings for bonds and deposits, as well as the government's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating, to Aaa, its highest grade, from Aa1. \par \par \uc2  The ratings agency said that the upgrade reflects continued strengthening of country's external financial position during the past several years, despite the Asian financial crisis and last year's economic downturn. Although Singapore's fiscal surplus has declined recently, Moody's noted that the government has very large holdings of financial and other assets and no foreign debt. \par \par \uc2  With the U.S. dollar having retreated significantly from a high of S$1.7945 Monday, market participants feared its continued decline may prompt the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the local dollar. \par \par \uc2  This caused foreign and local banks to buy U.S. dollars, lifting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  above S$1.7860. \par \par \uc2  Later in the session, the U.S. dollar reached an intraday high of S$1.7892, in line with its rebound above Y124.80 from Y124.50. The U.S. dollar's subsequent retreat below Y124.60 helped push it lower against the Singapore dollar as well. \par \par \uc2  "The volume has been very thin today and this has exaggerated the dollar's moves in either direction," an Asian bank dealer in Singapore said, explaining the relatively wide trading range. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expect the U.S. dollar to trade thinly between S$1.7820 and S$1.7920 in London and New York later Friday. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds rose sharply Friday, boosted by the Moody's upgrade and on media reports that a car bomb had exploded outside the U.S. consulate in Karachi killing at least five Pakistani nationals. Continued softness in interbank lending rates and a decline in local and regional equities markets, following the overnight fall on Wall Street, also boosted bonds. \par \par \uc2  Bonds opened higher tracking overnight gains in U.S. Treasurys and soared on the Moody's upgrade and the news of the Karachi explosion. \par \par \uc2  The yield on two-year bonds ended seven basis points lower at 1.41%, while the yield on five-year bonds fell 12 basis points to 2.75%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds fell 17 basis points to 3.25% and the yield on 10-year bonds fell 15 basis points to 3.65%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds fell 19 basis points to 4.06%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, swaps tracked local bond yields\par lower with the most liquid seven-year swap offer falling 15 basis points\par to 3.46% and the 10-year swap offer also slipping 16 basis points to\par 3.82%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between two- and 10-year swaps narrowed to 211 basis\par points, from 216 basis points late Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the local money market, term rates were flat amid flush liquidity\par in the banking system, while the overnight rate edged higher on\par pre-weekend demand for funds.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Friday       Late Thursday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.8125% 0.9375%   0.5625% 0.6875%\par 3-Month           0.6875% 0.8125%   0.6875% 0.8125%\par 1-Year            1.0000% 1.1250%   1.0625% 1.1250%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-64154-152;\par amit.prakash@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020614dy6e000mr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
