\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Mostly down on yen, rupiah eyes c.bank. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 760 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2002\par 04:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, June 5 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  down early Wednesday, tracking loses in the yen after \par \par \uc2  the Bank of Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     For the Philippine peso        and the Indonesian rupiah\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par , however, domestic factors were more in focus.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso was a little lower on Wednesday on political\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par worries while the rupiah traded cautiously below a nine-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par high set on Tuesday due to market fears the Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar eased to a session low of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.7890 per dollar, from late Tuesday's 1.7825, weighed down by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen's losses against the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the BOJ's fourth \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in two weeks had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par raised doubts over nearterm upside for the yen and other\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regionals which track Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as Japan is both a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par major market and export competitor for most Asian economies.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some corporate dollar sales for hedging needs was seen as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par likely to support Sing dollar around 1.7880-1.7890, but dealers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said some players were still short of dollars and may opt to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cover those positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht was down to 42.40, from late Tuesday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 42.29, with Singapore dealers expecting more downside on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regional yen issue. They said slowing equity and export-related\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows would also keep the baht depressed.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  HANGS OVER RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah strengthened to 8,575 per dollar from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lows around 8.650 seen late on Tuesday but this was still below\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a nine-month high set earlier on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers blamed the retreat on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  comments that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par some saw as opening the door to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to slow the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's appreciation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank Indonesia said it saw more room for the rupiah to rise\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this year but said it expected it to stabilise in the short\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's deputy governor Miranda Goeltom warned\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that it was important the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market did not overreact which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par could lead to excessive swings and affect economic recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Jakarta said players, most of whom were short of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars, took the comment as countering last month's statement\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par when the bank said that exports would remain competitive even\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par if the rupiah strengthened to 8,500 to the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah breached that early Tuesday to touch 8,440 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar - a level not seen since August 21 last year - but the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  comments led some players to fear \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MANILA FOCUS ON POLITICS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With Philippine May inflation figures issued in line with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expectations at an annual 3.6 percent, unchanged from April,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par analysts said the focus for the peso was on politics.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Samir Goel, market analyst at Bank of America in Singapore,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said economic numbers have taken a back seat after defection of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a Senator John Osmena to the opposition, tilting the balance in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Senate against President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This is an example yet again of how quickly political\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par factors can overtake the optimism on economic reforms in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Philippines, as in much of Southeast Asia," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Goel said opposition gaining majority in the upper house\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would heat up the political scene and could potentially delay\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the legislative process for some of the key reforms.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso quoted at around 50.60 to the dollar early\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday, against 50.43 close on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In May the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit a 13-month high of 49.20 to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar but it has come under pressure since then on worries\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over falling government revenues which could result in a higher\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par budget deficit.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.       $0223 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.94       123.38         -0.45\par  Sing dlr      1.7873       1.7825         -0.27\par  Taiwan dlr    34.091       34.093         +0.01\par  Korean won   1205.10      1220.10         +1.24\par  Baht           42.37        42.29         -0.19\par  Peso           50.59        50.43         -0.32\par  Rupiah       8575.00      8650.00         +0.87\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     123.94       131.24         +5.89\par  Sing dlr      1.7873       1.8515         +3.59\par  Taiwan dlr    34.091       34.986         +2.63\par  Korean won   1205.10      1277.00         +5.97\par  Baht           42.37        44.16         +4.22\par  Peso           50.59        51.50         +1.80\par  Rupiah       8575.00     10350.00        +20.70\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f2