\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Up Late Despite BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  In Yen Mkt \b0\par\par\uc2 582 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2002\par 11:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was stronger at the end of Asian trading Friday despite fresh attempts by the Bank of Japan to cap the yen's rise against the U.S. dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0911 GMT (5:11 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7844, down from S$1.7890 late Thursday. The U.S. dollar traded between S$1.7820 and S$1.7870 intraday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened around S$1.7855 against the Singapore dollar in Asia and then dropped to S$1.7830, as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slid against the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar fell to a session low of Y123.06 compared with its Thursday high of Y124.42, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar briefly spiked up to S$1.7870 against the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , following reports that the BOJ had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  But the U.S. dollar's rise was limited as market participants have been wary of such BOJ action since early Friday and have kept their positions thin, especially as the weekend approaches, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  retreated to its intraday low against the Singapore dollar late in the session as profit-taking from European-based market participants emerged, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, the U.S. dollar is likely to trade in a tight range against the local dollar, with its direction against the yen expected to set the trend, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is expected to be supported around S$1.7800, with resistance likely around S$1.7880. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds ended mostly higher Friday, tracking the overnight rise in U.S. Treasurys, though most tenors have been static since their early opening levels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said typically slow pre-weekend sentiment, a lack of market interest and the start of the soccer World Cup later Friday, together contributed to the thin trading volume in the local bond market. \par \par \uc2  The yield on two-year bonds was two basis points lower at 1.56%, while the yield on five-year bonds slipped one basis point to 2.94%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds also fell one basis point to 3.54% while the yield on 10-year bonds was steady at 3.93%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds was one basis point lower at 4.40%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, the most liquid seven-year swap\par offer was one basis point lower at 3.70% while the 10-year swap offer\par slipped one basis point at 4.07%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between two- and 10-year swaps narrowed to 217 basis points\par from 219 basis points late Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the local money market, rates were mostly steady as liquidity\par remained sufficient in the banking system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Friday       Late Thursday\par        