\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Firm, but restrained by BOJ threats. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Anchalee Worrachate \par \uc2 755 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2002\par 11:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 30 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held on to \par \par \uc2  their gains on Thursday, but regional bulls lacked the resolve \par \par \uc2  to push them higher amid threats of Bank of Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  as the dollar/yen languished near a recent defence line of 124. \par \par \uc2      Japanese monetary authorities had bought dollars twice last \par \par \uc2  week to curb the yen's appreciation around that level, and that \par \par \uc2  was partly why the market was getting jittery. \par \par \uc2      "But the yen could strengthen rapidly if it gets into the \par \par \uc2  123.70-124.10 zone without a BOJ response," said Ron Leven, \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Lehman Brothers in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2      Despite doubts about the economic recovery in the U.S. -- a \par \par \uc2  major market for Asian exports -- most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  largely underpinned by improving domestic economies. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar        rose past 1.7900, but it failed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to rise beyond 1.7880 where corporates and some local players\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ambushed the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Strategists said despite its recent rise, it was unlikely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (MAS) would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to rein in its gains as the Sing dollar was not out of sync\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON SHINES\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Korean won         -2 closed at 1,229.50 compared with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,234.20 at the open and Wednesday's closing of 1,234.30.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  finished below its intraday high as the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was wary of possible government moves after Finance and Economy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Minister Jeon Yun-churl told a gathering of economists that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par authorities were discussing appropriate steps regarding the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par won.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won has been having a ball lately, gaining 4.50 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par since the beginning of this month on a robust domestic economy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with data showing a strong pick up in industrial output -- a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par key barometer for exports performance.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts suggested that the Bank of Korea could become more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par aggressive in tightening monetary policy now that exports might\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par be strong enough to take over from domestic demand as a growth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par engine.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "When export is strong, it does not make sense for Korea to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par continue to leverage up just to keep the economy going at a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par double speed," said Andie Xie, regional economist for Morgan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Stanley in Hong Kong.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "A more sensible approach is to increase interest rates\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par aggressively to slow down household credit," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bumped up the key overnight rate target to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 4.25 percent from a record low of four percent in early May in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a pre-emptive move aimed at deflating a potential credit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bubble.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE Q1 GROWTH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippines' first quarter gross domestic product\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par numbers came in slightly lower than the market had expected,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but they failed to dampen sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GDP grew 3.8 percent year-on-year, in line with the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government's forecast range but below market expectations of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par about 4.1 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The weaker-than-expected growth was due to a smaller\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par contribution from net exports and slowing investment spending.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the market took heart from sustained growth in private\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par consumption which some economists estimate has accounted for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 70 percent of the Philippines' GDP.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso initially flinched to 50.00 after the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par numbers came out, but managed to rebound to close at 49.915 on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the back of firmer regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht rose to an intraday high of 42.38 -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its best level since February last year - but market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par participants were reluctant to push it much higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar/baht appeared oversold on charts, with a reading\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 23 on the 14-day relative strength index. The overbought\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par line is 30.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0808 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     124.07       124.44         +0.30\par  Sing dlr      1.7895       1.7918         +0.13\par  Taiwan dlr    34.190       34.239         +0.14\par  Korean won   1229.50      1234.24         +0.38\par  Baht           42.44        42.50         +0.14\par  Peso           49.89        50.07         +0.36\par  Rupiah       8825.00      8825.00         +0.00\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     124.07       131.24         +5.78\par  Sing dlr      1.7895       1.8515         +3.46\par  Korean won   1219.30      1277.00         +4.73\par  Baht           42.44        44.16         +4.05\par  Peso           49.89        51.50         +3.23\par  Rupiah       8825.00     10350.00        +17.28\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020530dy5u00jlo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
