\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Firm but under shadow of c.bank fears. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 832 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2002\par 11:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 29 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held \par \par \uc2  firm late Wednesday buoyed by the recent string of encouraging \par \par \uc2  economic data from across the region. \par \par \uc2      But with the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stuck in narrow ranges, \par \par \uc2  players in Asia feared pushing regionals higher could trigger \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from central banks. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar struggled against the yen       , edging\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slightly higher to around 124.55 yen from late New York trading\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lows of 124.49. It, however, retested eight-month lows hit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overnight beyond $0.93 against the euro .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Some dealers suspected the Bank of Korea bought dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par through local banks to slow the won's -2 rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "We believe that there was actual \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government since the Korean won has appreciated too rapidly,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said Frank Gong, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Bank of America\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in Hong Kong.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won surged to a session high of 1,229 per dollar, from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par late Tuesday's 1,237.5, before sliding back to a low of 1,243\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as local banks picked up dollars sparking talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GRADUAL RISE ACCEPTABLE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief Park Seung said a gradual rise in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the won was desirable in line with an economic rebound, but the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par speed of the gain needed to be checked.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "I think a gradual rise in the won is desirable within a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range that doesn't affect exports," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     That helped the won to end onshore trade at 1,234.3. Early\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains were backed by a surprise rise in April industrial\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par production of 1.8 percent on the month and a fall in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par current account surplus to $30 million from $1.04 billion in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par March.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Those numbers were seen reflecting a sharp pick up in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic activity and supported hopes of a robust growth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outlook.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Impressed by the won and helped by month-end dollar sales\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by exporters, the Taiwan dollar hit a fresh 11-=\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par month peak at 34.23.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But fears of aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar purchases made\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players reluctant to push the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  much higher. Onshore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade ended slightly firmer at 34.239, against Tuesday's close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 34.309.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PESO SEEN FAIRLY VALUED\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso ended steady at 50.07 after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par touching session highs at 49.90. The gains were cut short by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar purchases to meet debt payment\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par needs.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Rafael Buenaventura said in an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interview the peso was fairly valued at its current 49-50 range\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and could rise up to 48, depending on the direction other\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might take.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Persistent dollar purchases by local banks mostly on behalf\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of corporate clients capped the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 1.7920.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Lingering wariness over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the yen by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese authorities also kept players from probing last week's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 7-=   month highs of 1.7855 on the Sing dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But overall sentiment was still supportive backed by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday's manufacturing production numbers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Production rose a surprise 8.1 percent in April from a year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par earlier, marking the strongest growth in 12 months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     RUPIAH & BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Indonesian rupiah        rose to fresh nine-month highs\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 8,820, from late Tuesday's 8,850.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Still players were a bit cautious ahead of an expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par announcement on the sale of Bank Niaga .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Two consortia are in the final bidding but Indonesian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par authorities have warned they might call off the sale if final\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bids were too low compared with the bank's market price.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht bumped against fresh 15-month highs at 42.50\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par beyond which the market fears the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may step in to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cap gains that were mainly driven by equity-related inflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Thai Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak said on Wednesday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic recovery was on the right track and did not need\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par additional stimulus measures.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Somkid's comments came after the International Monetary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fund on Tuesday raised its projection for Thai 2002 gross\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic product growth to 3.2 percent from 2.7 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.       $0904 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     124.44       124.49         +0.04\par  Sing dlr      1.7918       1.7929         +0.06\par  Taiwan dlr    34.239       34.309         +0.20\par  Korean won   1233.90      1237.50         +0.29\par  Baht           42.50        42.57         +0.16\par  Peso           50.03        50.07         +0.08\par  Rupiah       8825.00      8850.00         +0.28\par  Ringgit     