\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Firm on weak dlr sentiment, strong data. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 800 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2002\par 04:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 29 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  firm early on Wednesday, encouraged by a dollar seen vulnerable \par \par \uc2  against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and with data supporting \par \par \uc2  regional optimism that an economic rebound is gathering \par \par \uc2  momentum. \par \par \uc2      "While dollar's underlying sentiment is still weak, data \par \par \uc2  from across the region has showed that not only an export \par \par \uc2  recovery has begun but there are signs of some life in domestic \par \par \uc2  demand," a senior dealer at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2      The latest in a slew of favourable data came from Korea, \par \par \uc2  where April industrial output rose a surprise 1.8 percent on \par \par \uc2  the month and the current account surplus fell to $30 million \par \par \uc2  from $1.04 billion in March. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Korean won         -2 rose to 1,229 per dollar, from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday's late 1,237.5, on the figures, which were seen as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par evidence of robust growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Though fears of dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by authorities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would keep \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains limited, dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overall sentiment was bullish.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN AT FRESH HIGHS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar          touched an 11-=   month high of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 32.237, against late Tuesday's 34.309, backed by the upbeat\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regional mood and equity-related foreign inflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore said the Taiwan dollar continues to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par defy repeated aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par so far managed to only smooth out excessive volatility.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Taiwan's index of leading indicators for April, released on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Monday, rose for the seventh straight month to a 20-month high.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar        was trading around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.7930-1.7940, little changed from late Tuesday's 1.7929 and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par still far from its 7-=   month highs of 1.7855 hit last week,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but with sentiment supported by Tuesday's manufacturing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par production data for April.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     An 8.1 percent rise on the year in production overshot\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market forecasts and was seen a showing the recovery was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gaining pace.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said talk of dollar bids by local banks around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.7920 were limiting gains, but overall sentiment was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par supportive of the Sing dollar with downside seen capped at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 1.7950.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They said lingering fears of the Bank of Japan's\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap the yen's gains was also keeping players\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cautious.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par IMF AIDS BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht was little changed at 42.55, against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday's late 42.57, focusing on news late on Tuesday that the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par International Monetary Fund has raised its 2002 forecast of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thai economic growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The IMF said it had raised the forecast to 3.2 percent from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2.7 percent, based on strong consumer demand and recovering\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par global economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thailand's finance ministry expects 2002 GDP growth of 3.6\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent, while the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's has projected a 2.5-3.5\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, the Thai commerce ministry late on Tuesday also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par raised its 2002 export forecast to 5.6 percent from 5.0\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said baht was likely to stay supported\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by a recent surge in equity-related inflows. Foreign investors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Tuesday bought net 1.895 billion baht worth of local stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But fears of Bank of Thailand dollar purchases beyond 42.50\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par baht were likely to keep gains limited.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     RUPIAH CAUTIOUS, PESO UP\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Indonesian rupiah        rose to 8,830, from Tuesday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par late 8,850, with players cautious ahead of expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par announcement on that sale of Bank Niaga later in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Two consortia are in the final round, but Indonesian\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par authorities have said they will call off the sale if bids are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par too low compared with the bank's market price.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso was up at 49.91 per dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against Tuesday's onshore close of 50.07, with sentiment buoyed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by Tuesday's first quarter production index that rose for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par first time in three quarters.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.       $0150 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     124.63       124.49         -0.11\par  Sing dlr      1.7933       1.7929         -0.02\par  Taiwan dlr    34.258       34.309         +0.15\par  Korean won   1222.50      1237.50         +1.23\par  Baht           42.57        42.57         +0.00\par  Peso           49.94        50.07         +0.26\par  Rupiah       8830.00      8850.00         +0.23\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     124.63       131.24         +5.30\par  Sing dlr      1.7933       1.8515         +3.25\par  Taiwan dlr    34.258       34.986         +2.13\par  Korean won   1222.50      1277.00         +4.46\par  Baht           42.57        44.16         +3.74\par  Peso           49.94        51.50         +3.12\par  Rupiah       8830.00     10350.00        +17.21\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020529dy5t004mp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\p