\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Southeast track won, Taiwan dlr gains. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 786 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2002\par 05:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 28 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed up \par \par \uc2  early on Tuesday, taking their cue from a steadier yen and \par \par \uc2  local factors, though lingering fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities against their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to \par \par \uc2  limit gains. \par \par \uc2      The Korean won hit a fresh 17-month high and the Taiwan \par \par \uc2  dollar rose to 11-=   month peaks. \par \par \uc2      Dealers in Singapore said players in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \par \par \uc2  including the yen, would be less aggressive ahead of consumer \par \par \uc2  data from the United States. \par \par \uc2      But if April personal income and spending numbers and May's \par \par \uc2  conference board consumer confidence index support the dollar, \par \par \uc2  dealers said that would be taken only as an opportunity to sell \par \par \uc2  the greenback. \par \par \uc2  "Given the current bullish sentiment towards the yen, any \par \par \uc2  rebound of the dollar would be unsustainable, and should be \par \par \uc2  taken as an opportunities to sell the dollar," a senior dealer \par \par \uc2  at a Singapore bank said. \par \par \uc2  He said historically, over the last decade, bounces in the \par \par \uc2  Japanese economy accompany equity-related inflows which in turn \par \par \uc2  push the yen higher and snuff out the economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  "The Japanese authorities are well aware of this fact but \par \par \uc2  how far they are prepared to go (to limit the yen's gains) is \par \par \uc2  still a matter of speculation," said the dealer, whose bank \par \par \uc2  forecast the yen would hit 120 per dollar in a few weeks' time. \par \par \uc2  NORTH LEADS \par \par \uc2  The bullish view on the yen coupled with growing optimism \par \par \uc2  that most regional economies in Asia would outperform other \par \par \uc2  emerging markets have been supporting sentiment in regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other Asian assets. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said recently the North Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  getting an extra boost from month-end dollar sales by \par \par \uc2  exporters. \par \par \uc2  The Korean won hit a fresh 17-month high at 1,226 per \par \par \uc2  dollar, up more than a percent from late Monday's 1,233.8 and \par \par \uc2  shrugging off recent verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the authorities. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the market was more focused on \par \par \uc2  April industrial output numbers due on Wednesday and May \par \par \uc2  consumer price data on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar, cheering the release of positive \par \par \uc2  economic data, rose to 11-= month highs at 34.275 per dollar, \par \par \uc2  from late Monday's 34.375. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan said late on Monday the index of leading indicators \par \par \uc2  for April rose for the seventh straight month to a 20-month \par \par \uc2  high. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said equity-related inflows were also \par \par \uc2  backing those gains although dollar purchases from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were seen capping gains for now. \par \par \uc2  SOUTHEAST TO CATCH UP \par \par \uc2  In the southeast, the Singapore dollar and Thai baht jumped \par \par \uc2  in an attempt to catch up with the gains in the north as trade \par \par \uc2  resumed there after a long weekend. \par \par \uc2      Both Singapore and Thailand were closed on Monday for local \par \par \uc2  holidays. \par \par \uc2      The Singapore dollar rose to levels just shy of 1.7900 per \par \par \uc2  dollar, from levels around 1.7980 on Friday, following gains in \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of export rivals Korea and Taiwan. \par \par \uc2      But some profit-taking and local commercial dollar demand \par \par \uc2  pulled the Sing dollar back to levels around 1.7930. \par \par \uc2      April industrial production data due later in the day was \par \par \uc2  expected to confirm a tentative rebound is gathering momentum, \par \par \uc2  after recent strong export figures for April. \par \par \uc2      The Sing dollar is still some way from its 7-1/2-month high \par \par \uc2  of 1.785 hit last Wednesday before physical \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  against the yen prompted players to cover their short dollar \par \par \uc2  positions. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht strengthened to a session high of 42.60 \par \par \uc2  before some profit-taking by local interbank players pulled it \par \par \uc2  back to levels around 42.70, though that was still higher than \par \par \uc2  last Friday's 42.82, before the market's long weekend. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said the Thai market would track gains \par \par \uc2  in the Singapore dollar and other regionals, though fears of \par \par \uc2  potential dollar purchases by the Bank of Thailand and talk of \par \par \uc2  local dollar bids around 42.50-42.60 was likely to limit the \par \par \uc2  upside. \par \par \uc2  Buyers of the Indonesian rupiah kept their fingers crossed \par \par \uc2  ahead of an expected announcement of the winner of a \par \par \uc2  majority-stake in the state's Bank Niaga. \par \par \uc2  The level of final bids by the two bidders left in the race \par \par \uc2  could send an important signal about investor confidence. If \par \par \uc2  the bids are at too great a discount to the market price of the \par \par \uc2  bank's shares, Indonesian authorities might abandon the \par \par \uc2  auction. \par \par \uc2      The rupiah hit a peak of 8,845 per dollar, a level last \par \par \uc2  seen on September 12. \par \par \uc2      The Philippine peso also gained to test the 50 per dollar \par \par \uc2  level, encouraged by the gains in the other regionals. It hit a \par \par \uc2  session high of 50.08, from late Monday's 50.53. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020528dy5s005vb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
