\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Flinch on BOJ threats, data eyed. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Anchalee Worrachate \par \uc2 765 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2002\par 11:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 24 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended the \par \par \uc2  week on a jittery note, after the Bank of Japan sent the market \par \par \uc2  a multi-billion dollar message that they are not going to take \par \par \uc2  the yen's rapid rise sitting down. \par \par \uc2      The BoJ bought dollars to rein in the yen on Wednesday and \par \par \uc2  Thursday for the first time since September, forcing traders to \par \par \uc2  cover short positions. \par \par \uc2      Some dealers estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent $2-3 billion \par \par \uc2  on the first day and $1-2 billion on the second, while others \par \par \uc2  said it could have spent $5-6 billion on the first round \par \par \uc2  alone. \par \par \uc2   Dealers said Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were now pretty squarish \par \par \uc2  and most were reluctant to be aggressive on either side of the \par \par \uc2  fence ahead of a long Memorial Day holiday weekend in the U.S. \par \par \uc2      "The BOJ will have little difficulty in supporting the \par \par \uc2  dollar through the long U.S. holiday weekend, but how they \par \par \uc2  behave after Monday should also shed light on their \par \par \uc2  determination to hold current levels," said Ron Leven, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  strategist at Lehman Brothers in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2      The market was trapped between wariness of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on one side and traders wanting to sell the \par \par \uc2  dollar on heightened fears of terror attacks in the U.S. \par \par \uc2      Fresh violence in Israel and Japanese exporters with \par \par \uc2  substantial dollars to sell above 125 yen were also seen \par \par \uc2  keeping pressure on the dollar. \par \par \uc2      The market is watching out for a raft of data, starting \par \par \uc2  with U.S. first quarter gross domestic product figures due \par \par \uc2  later on Friday. Economists polled by Reuters expect GDP to be \par \par \uc2  revised up to 6.0 percent from 5.8 percent. \par \par \uc2      Next week, Taiwan is scheduled to release its leading \par \par \uc2  economic indicator which analysts said was likely to confirm a \par \par \uc2  pick up in activity. \par \par \uc2      The Philippines publishes its first quarter gross domestic \par \par \uc2  product data on May 31. A Reuters poll predicted the economy \par \par \uc2  had grown around 3.6-5.0 percent in that period, compared with \par \par \uc2  the government's target of 3.8-4.2 percent. \par \par \uc2      PESO SOGGY \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippine peso        led regional losers on Friday,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par finishing at 50.35 to the dollar -- its worst closing level\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par since May 2 -- compared with 49.84 in the previous session.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Trading was brisk, with $220.50 million transacted.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Manila said corporate players, especially oil\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par companies, piled in to buy dollars on views that perhaps the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BoJ's latest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might be providing a floor for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The market was pretty short in the first place. The BoJ's\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  just provide participants with an excuse to adjust\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par their positions," said a dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "And the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's remarks on the peso did not help\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par either."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Rafael Buenaventura said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Friday the peso's slide to 50 was not worrisome and that the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank had not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BAHT, SING DOLLAR SOFT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht        and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar        were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par also weaker as players pared short dollar positions, fearing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par they might get caught on the wrong side of the market when they\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par return from a long weekend holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Financial markets in Thailand and Singapore will be closed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Monday for a religious holiday. They will reopen on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht languished around 42.85 late on Friday, with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exporters holding off dollar offers on speculation the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would rise further from here.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar trimmed early losses on the strength of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par euro and the Indonesian rupiah - its major\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading partners - but failed to pull back into positive\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par territory.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traded around 1.7990 late on Friday compared\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with 1.8010 earlier in the day.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0656 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     125.03       124.19         -0.67\par  Sing dlr      1.7987       1.7958         -0.16\par  Taiwan dlr    34.411       34.383         -0.08\par  Korean won   1249.50      1246.10         -0.27\par  Baht           42.84        42.81         -0.07\par  Peso           50.10        49.84         -0.52\par  Rupiah       8963.00      8980.00         +0.19\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     125.03       131.24         +4.97\par  Sing dlr      1.7987       1.8515         +2.94\par  Korean won   1249.50      1277.00         +2.20\par  Baht           42.84        44.16         +3.08\par  Peso           50.10        51.50         +2.79\par  Rupiah       8963.00     10350.00        +15.47\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020524dy5o00jlz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
