\par\par \b \uc2  Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Up Late; BOJ Checks Yen Strength \b0\par\par\uc2  By Alan Yonan Jr. \par \uc2 1,186 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2002\par 12:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities to check the yen's strength helped the dollar gain modestly against most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although analysts said the dollar's weakness is likely to persist in the near term. \par \par \uc2  The surprise \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan boosted the dollar by more than one full yen in afternoon trading and helped the beleaguered U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regain some of its recent losses across Asia. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished higher against the Singapore dollar, Thai baht, Philippine peso and Indonesian rupiah. The South Korean won and New Taiwan dollar shrugged off the dollar's bounce to post 15- and 11-month highs, respectively. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had expressed concerns that excessive yen strength could derail the country's nascent economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  The yen has appreciated nearly 8% since the end of March, hitting an seven-month high of Y123.51 per dollar Wednesday. Some traders estimated that the BOJ bought at least US$1 billion, sending the dollar from Y123.70 to a high of Y125.10 in a matter of minutes. \par \par \uc2  "Recent movements of exchange rates have been too rapid," Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said in a prepared statement following the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We will continue to closely monitor the market and take appropriate action as necessary." \par \par \uc2  The dollar held relatively firm for the balance of the session, finishing Asian trading hours at Y124.90, compared with Y124.07 late Tuesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  However, the pressure that the dollar is experiencing in global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets is expected to continue, given investors' concerns about U.S. assets and the resulting flow of capital out of U.S. markets. \par \par \uc2  Data compiled by UBS Warburg showed that net outflows of equity-related capital for the week ended May 17 totaled US$277 million, the fifth net outflow in six weeks. The Asia-Pacific, meanwhile, enjoyed its largest inflows since mid-February. \par \par \uc2  "This is troubling news for dollar bulls given the U.S.'s need for capital inflows to fund its current account deficit. It also explains the recent dollar weakness," UBS Warburg said in a report. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. current account deficit stands at 4.2% of gross domestic product and US$1 billion in capital inflows is required each day to finance the shortfall. \par \par \uc2  The yen's retracement triggered some short covering of dollars against the won, not enough to keep the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from barreling to its strongest finish since February 2001. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at 1,247.2 won, compared with KRW1,254.6 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Government officials repeated warnings to market players about excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements, keeping the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fresh on their minds. \par \par \uc2  Vice Minister of Finance and Economy Yoon Jin-Shik said the government was "greatly concerned" about the won's rise. Bank of Korea Governor Park Seung later added that while there was no need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the moment, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was prepared to do so if the won appreciated too sharply. \par \par \uc2  The government has made such statements in recent days every time the won strengthens by more than 0.5% against the dollar, Roger Yip, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of America noted. \par \par \uc2  Because the warnings have been somewhat effective, the authorities have not felt the need to actually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Yip added. \par \par \uc2  The yen's fall and sporadic U.S.-dollar buying by importers dealt a brief setback to the New Taiwan dollar. \par \par \uc2  "But the outlook for the yen and NT dollar remains bright in the near term because Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely only be temporary and foreign equity funds are continuing to flee the U.S. to Europe and Asia," a local bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar ended at NT$34.393, compared with NT$34.415 at the previous close. It was the strongest close for the New Taiwan dollar since June 2001. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowered a key open market rate, sending a signal that it remains cautious about the economic recovery and that it is worried the strength of the New Taiwan dollar could threaten exports. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said cutting the offered rate on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily 14- and 28-day negotiable certificates of deposit and CDs effectively loosens monetary policy although it didn't act through its usual policy instruments. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar weakened along with the yen following the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Late in Asia, the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7940, up from S$1.7930 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar slipped to a low of S$1.7865 in early trading but recovered as market players became concerned that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide. The U.S. dollar rise accelerated later in the day following the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was not overly concerned that movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets would derail Asia's economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  With global inventories being replenished and demand for information technology products beginning to recover, "this momentum is unlikely to be significantly affected by short-term volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets," the MAS said. \par \par \uc2  The peso relinquished its early gains as traders scrambled to cover short-dollar positions after the Japanese government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stall the yen's advance. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at its intraday high of 49.79 pesos on the Philippine Dealing System, up from PHP49.465 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's close was also a dramatic reversal from its opening level of PHP49.25 - a 14-month low. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah surged to an eight-month high in early trading, but gave up its gains later in the session, partly due to the yen's decline. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened on the defensive and quickly fell through 9,000 rupiah on its way to a low of IDR8,905, its weakest performance since last September. \par \par \uc2  The dollar then climbed steadily through the session to finish Asian trading at IDR9,055, up from IDR9,030 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that the dollar didn't stay below IDR9,000 for a long time reflected that people aren't yet fully comfortable with holding excessive dollar-short positions below that level," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Investors may be getting ahead of themselves with their exuberance over Indonesia's privatization program, said Sameer Goel, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of America. \par \par \uc2  While progress on reforms may help the rupiah strengthen over the near term, investing in Indonesia still carries considerable risks, he said. \par \par \uc2  "Investors should be cautious. The rupiah will likely be weaker by the end of the year rather than stronger," Goel said. \par \par \uc2  The baht succumbed to the yen's late session weakness. \par \par \uc2  Near the end of Asian trading the dollar was quoted at 42.810 baht, up from THB42.670 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Corporate dollar buying for debt repayments also weighed on the baht. \par \par \uc2  -By Alan Yonan Jr., Dow Jones Newswires; 65 9862-0905; alan.yonan@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020522dy5m000mj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
