\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Higher Late; Hit Fresh 7-Mo Peak Intraday \b0\par\par\uc2 639 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 2002\par 11:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar was higher late Monday on follow-through U.S. dollar selling which began Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was "comfortable" with the current level of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A stronger yen also helped boost the Singapore dollar against its U.S. counterpart. \par \par \uc2  Around 0833 GMT (4:33 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.7906, down from S$1.7950 late Friday. It traded between S$1.7886 and S$1.7950 intraday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar opened flat in Asia and fell steadily until midmorning on selling by interbank market participants and brokers. The U.S. dollar found an intraday floor at a fresh seven-month low of S$1.7886 amid fears that excessively sharp exchange rate moves may provoke the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  into \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reduce volatility. \par \par \uc2  Monday's sharp drop in the U.S. dollar was also attributed to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's persistent weakness against the yen. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped below Y126 in Asia Monday to a low so far of Y125.35, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone's just getting out of their longs because MAS hasn't come in to defend the (U.S.) dollar after it fell below S$1.8000 on Friday," a European bank dealer in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the U.S. dollar touched a session low of S$1.7940 against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a senior official from the MAS said it was comfortable with current level of the Singapore dollar. That was after a quarterly economic survey Friday which confirmed market beliefs that the economy is on the recovery path. \par \par \uc2  Market participants took the statement to mean that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might tolerate a stronger local dollar, coming at a time when the U.S. dollar is on a weakening bias against other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers cite subsequent support for the U.S. dollar at S$1.7880 against the local dollar amid \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears, with resistance at S$1.7940. \par \par \uc2  "We expect selling on rallies toward S$1.7940 because everyone is still keen on selling the (U.S.) dollar," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds fell Monday in line with Friday's sharp fall in U.S. Treasurys. \par \par \uc2  The yield on the two-year bond rose six basis points to 1.63% and the five-year bond yield was three basis points higher at 3.0%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds was up five basis points at 3.62%, while the yield on 10-year bonds inched up four basis points to 3.97%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds rose three basis points to 4.45%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, rates edged higher, tracking local\par bond yields.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The most liquid seven-year swap offer rise nine basis point to 3.81%\par while the 10-year swap offer rose six basis points to 4.15%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between two- and 10-year swaps narrowed to 216 basis points\par from 217 basis points late Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the local money market, rates were mostly steady amid ample\par liquidity in the banking system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Monday       Late Friday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.8750% 1.0000%   0.7500% 0.8750%\par 3-Month           0.8125% 0.8750%   0.8125% 0.8750%\par 1-Year            1.1250% 1.2500%   1.1250% 1.2500%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Amit Prakash, Dow Jones Newswires; +65-6415-4152;\par amit.prakash@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020520dy5k000gi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
