\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  habit seen fading on recovery hopes. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 640 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2002\par 09:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , May 17 (Reuters) - Asian policymakers are well known for trying to steer \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  From setting up \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pegs to direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , central bankers from Bangkok to Seoul have a well-deserved reputation for manoeuvring to keep their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at preferred levels. \par \par \uc2  Thus, it comes as no surprise the recent weakness in the U.S. dollar, and especially since early April, has spurred central banks to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to temper strength in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts say the bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may soon fade, reflecting growing optimism about an economic recovery,twinned with the relative weakness in the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against those of other major trading partners - Europe and Japan. \par \par \uc2  UNDERPERFORMED YEN \par \par \uc2  "Some of these Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have underperformed the yen and euro as they rallied, making sure that on a trade-weighted basis they haven't really gone up," said David Simmonds, Salomon Smith Barney's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Trade-weighted exchange rates show the value of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its trading partners. \par \par \uc2  Though Simmonds believes central banks will keep the markets on their toes with verbal threats, the chances of actual \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are small. \par \par \uc2  "Most central banks are reasonably relaxed with the recent gains," he added. \par \par \uc2  This view was underlined on Friday when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore said the local dollar's recent strength had not pushed it out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's actively managed policy band, used to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  competitive. \par \par \uc2  "Although the Sing dollar had appreciated...the Sing dollar is still within the band," MAS senior director Khor Hoe Ee said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players saw the comments as a green light for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to further appreciate and took the Singapore dollar to a seven-month high. \par \par \uc2  VERBAL NOT REAL \par \par \uc2  It may take time, though, to wean policymakers completely off the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  habit. \par \par \uc2  A South Korean finance ministry official, also on Friday, said Korea was ready to rein in the won's sharp rise, although most analysts saw that as an effort in micro manage market expectations rather than a real threat and the won rose to a new five-month peak. \par \par \uc2  The warning followed remarks from Commerce Minister Shin Kook-hwan that he expected the won to strengthen to 1,250 per U.S. dollar in the second half of 2002 versus around 1,265 now. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said with the yen/won cross almost unchanged at around 9.8 Korean won since early April, there was scant chance of any market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In a region where exports account for about half of the total gross domestic product and foreign investment is seen as one of the major drivers of growth, maintaining exchange rate competitiveness is a top priority for policy-makers. \par \par \uc2  UNDERVALUED VS DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Geoffrey Barker, chief economist of HSBC in Hong Kong, said that on an inflation-adjusted basis most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were still 15 to 20 percent undervalued against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  "There is no doubt that the rise in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far does not leave them expensive," he said. \par \par \uc2  Simmonds, meanwhile, said that while the trade-weighted yen is still down by about five percent over the last 12 months, it has gained some 3.5 percent in the recent rally against dollar. \par \par \uc2  The euro in the same period has gained about 2 percent in trade-weighted terms. \par \par \uc2  On the same scale and period, most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have only slightly appreciated. In fact, several of them are weaker from levels where they were 12 months back, with the Taiwan dollar down six percent and Singapore dollar off about three percent. \par \par \uc2  In contrast, on a nominal basis the Taiwan dollar is up by about five percent since May 2001 and the Singapore dollar has gained more than one percent. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020517dy5h00fgh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
