\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Higher Late, But Keeps To Very Tight Range \b0\par\par\uc2 690 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Mai 2002\par 10:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar strengthened against its U.S. counterpart late Monday, but held to a very tight trading range as market participants couldn't establish a clear direction from other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0815 GMT (4:15 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.8035, down from S$1.8070 late Friday. It traded between S$1.8025 and S$1.8040 intraday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened around S$1.8025 in Asia and hovered in a tight range of between S$1.8025 and S$1.8035 throughout most of the session on a lack of fresh market-moving leads, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar briefly rose an intraday high of S$1.8040 mid-afternoon, but this was due mainly to a bout of U.S. dollar buying against other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially the yen. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar rise was triggered by its ascent to Y127.45 against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but fizzled out when it failed to reach its early Asian high of Y127.70, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said overall market sentiment was still negative towards the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with many intent on selling U.S. dollars on rallies on concerns over the unit's near-term resilience. \par \par \uc2  Still, the Singapore dollar's strength was limited by concerns that excessive moves would draw \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which guides the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar within a trading band against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the country's major trading partners. \par \par \uc2  "The overall (U.S.) dollar picture is still weak, but there is a bit of caution (in the local market) especially when we get too close to S$1.8000," a European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Last week, after the U.S. dollar dropped to a seven-month low of S$1.7988 against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , local banks aggressively bought U.S. dollars, lifting it to around S$1.8020 and sparking concerns they were acting on behalf of the MAS. \par \par \uc2  Overnight, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to gradually drift lower against its Singapore counterpart, although this would depend on the U.S. dollar's persistent weakness against other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Support for the U.S. dollar is expected at S$1.8000, with resistance at S$1.8050. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds were mostly higher late Monday, lifted by gains in U.S. Treasurys late Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Local bonds were also boosted by the persistent weakness of domestic interbank rates, some of which have been hovering near historic lows for more than a month, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yield on two-year bonds was down three basis points at 1.53%, while the yield on five-year bonds shed six basis points to 2.91%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yield on seven-year bonds slipped four basis points to 3.54%, while the yield on 10-year bonds was three basis points lower at 3.91%. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds was three basis points lower at 4.40%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, swaps tracked local bond yields\par lower with the seven-year swap offer slipping two basis points to 3.71%\par while the 10-year swap offer shed one basis points to 4.08%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between two- and 10-year swaps widened to 220 from 219\par basis points late Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the local money market rates maintained their soft tone as\par liquidity remained sufficient in the banking system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Monday       Late Friday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.6875% 0.7500%   0.6875% 0.7500%\par 3-Month           0.7500% 0.8750%   0.7500% 0.8750%\par 1-Year            1.0625% 1.1875%   1.1250% 1.2500%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-64154-157;\par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020513dy5d000mx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
