\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Squeezed as overweight market trims fat. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Anchalee Worrachate \par \uc2 769 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2002\par 11:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 8 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  pared some of \par \par \uc2  their recent gains on Wednesday as players covered short dollar \par \par \uc2  positions after strong data and stabilising equity markets in \par \par \uc2  the United States left dollar bears feeling exposed. \par \par \uc2      But strategists cautioned the dollar's rebound should not \par \par \uc2  be taken as a sign of a turnaround yet as U.S. assets, a key \par \par \uc2  ingredient to the dollar's strength, remain generally weak. \par \par \uc2      "I've never been that bearish about the dollar. But that \par \par \uc2  said, I don't really have signals in place that I'm looking for \par \par \uc2  to be able to pound the table and say 'go out to buy the dollar \par \par \uc2  today'," said Ron Leven, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Lehman \par \par \uc2  Brothers. \par \par \uc2      The Singapore dollar retreated to 1.8075 after surging to a \par \par \uc2  seven-month high of 1.7980 in the previous session, as players \par \par \uc2  bought back U.S. dollars on fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  and as the dollar rebounded. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic recovery is still fragile and many in \par \par \uc2  the market are convinced it is unlikely the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \par \par \uc2  allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate sharply. \par \par \uc2      The Indonesian rupiah came off intraday lows of 9,310 after \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  painted a bright economic picture for the \par \par \uc2  second quarter, but the good news failed to jolt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  into positive territory due to strong corporate demand for \par \par \uc2  dollars. \par \par \uc2      It said in a statement obtained by Reuters that the country \par \par \uc2  was likely to grow by 3.5-4.0 percent in the April-June period \par \par \uc2  on the back of domestic demand, with the balance of payments \par \par \uc2  outlook also improving. \par \par \uc2      "The main theme today is still the dollar's movement \par \par \uc2  against majors and short covering. The numbers from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  look good, but I don't think people are completely \par \par \uc2  surprised by them,"  said a rupiah non-deliverable forwards \par \par \uc2  dealer in Singapore. \par \par \uc2      DOLLAR'S REBOUND \par \par \uc2      The bruised dollar clambered off its multi-month lows \par \par \uc2  against majors and Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , thanks to strong U.S. data \par \par \uc2  which showed first quarter productivity was up 8.6 percent on \par \par \uc2  an annualised basis -- its fastest pace in almost 19 years. \par \par \uc2      The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also drew support from news that Cisco \par \par \uc2  Systems Inc -- the world's biggest maker of equipment that \par \par \uc2  powers the Internet -- reported its quarterly profits more than \par \par \uc2  tripled last year's results and beat Wall Street estimates. \par \par \uc2      Rumours that the Bank of Japan was in the market overnight \par \par \uc2  to check rates also boosted the dollar. \par \par \uc2      It rose to a one-week high against the yen to around \par \par \uc2  128.50. The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is closely tracked by the \par \par \uc2  regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      KOREAN WON, BAHT \par \par \uc2      The won 2 flinched, closing at 1,285.40 against  Tuesday's \par \par \uc2  close of 1,279.50, which had been its highest since \par \par \uc2  mid-December. \par \par \uc2      Wariness of potential \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar-buying \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and foreign demand for the dollar in the wake of \par \par \uc2  recent selling in local stocks weighed on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      But its downside was limited by news that the government \par \par \uc2  was stepping up its privatisation drive, which raised hopes for \par \par \uc2  more capital inflows. \par \par \uc2      The Thai baht was a whisker away from the 43 level which it \par \par \uc2  managed to break for the first time since end-February last \par \par \uc2  year. \par \par \uc2      Market participants appeared reluctant to buy the Thai \par \par \uc2  authorities' story that they were not concerned about the \par \par \uc2  baht's strength at this point. \par \par \uc2      The Taiwan dollar drew little support from trade data which \par \par \uc2  showed the island's exports rose 0.3 percent in April on the \par \par \uc2  year to US$10.876 billion, as it was pretty much in line with \par \par \uc2  market consensus. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at 34.588 against 34.565 on Tuesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. $0803 GMT \par \par \uc2  Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     128.40       127.64         -0.59\par  Sing dlr      1.8085       1.8040         -0.25\par  Taiwan dlr    34.588       34.565         -0.07\par  Korean won   1285.40      1279.50         -0.46\par  Baht           42.91        42.85         -0.14\par  Peso           49.79        49.64         -0.30\par  Rupiah       9290.00      9285.00         -0.05\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     128.40       131.24         +2.21\par  Sing dlr      1.8085       1.8515         +2.38\par  Korean won   1269.50      1277.00         +0.59\par  Baht           42.91        44.16         +2.91\par  Peso           49.79        51.50         +3.43\par  Rupiah       9290.00     10350.00        +11.41\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020508dy5800hfw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
