\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dlr Down Late As Yen, Regional  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Slip \b0\par\par\uc2 687 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2002\par 10:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The Singapore dollar fell against the U.S. dollar late Wednesday, in line with a weakening of the yen and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0830 GMT (4:30 a.m. EDT), the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.8092, up from S$1.8023 late Tuesday. It traded between S$1.8060 and S$1.8095 intraday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also benefited from worries about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened around S$1.8090 against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia, after trimming part of its recent losses against the yen overnight, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The widely expected decision by the U.S. Federal Reserve's policy-setting body, the Federal Open Market Committee, to keep U.S. interest rates steady was taken in stride by market participants and didn't trigger any major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements in Asia, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar slipped early in the session. However, it recovered slightly after a late bout of yen selling dragged down other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the Singapore dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar broke through its overnight high of Y128.39 to reach an Asian session high of Y128.45, from an intraday low of Y127.80. \par \par \uc2  Market participants in Singapore initially refrained from selling the U.S. dollar amid talk that the MAS had aggressively bought U.S. dollars, after the unit U.S. fell to a seven-month low against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The MAS uses the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rather than interest rates, as its primary monetary-policy tool in seeking to maintain brisk growth and low inflation. The Singapore dollar is guided within a trading band against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the country's major trading partners. \par \par \uc2  Still, European market participants took advantage of the light activity to cover their short U.S. dollar positions as the Asian trading day neared its close, dealers added. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, the U.S. dollar is expected to retreat slightly as market participants take profit in overnight trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Support for the U.S. dollar is expected at S$1.8060, with resistance likely at S$1.8120. \par \par \uc2  Prices of Singapore government bonds succumbed to modest profit-taking to end the session slightly lower after an early morning rise, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Local bonds rose early on overnight gains in U.S. Treasurys, after bond market sentiment was lifted by U.S. policymakers' cautious tone on near-term U.S. economic recovery, dealers added. \par \par \uc2  However prices slipped as selling pressure emerged late in the local afternoon session, although trading volume stayed moderate, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yield on two-year bonds was up one basis point at 1.55%, while the yield on five-year bonds inched up two basis points to 2.92%. \par \par \uc2  At the longer end of the curve, the yields on seven-year bonds and 10-year bonds were both one basis point higher at 3.54% and 3.88%, respectively. \par \par \uc2  The yield on 15-year bonds also rose one basis point to 4.38%. \par \par \uc2  The above are pre-settlement closing bids obtained from dealers and are subject to minor changes. Historical bond yields and prices can be viewed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the interest rate swaps market, swaps were mixed with the\par seven-year swap offer rising two basis points to 3.71% while the 10-year\par swap offer held steady at 4.05%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spread between two- and 10-year swaps narrowed slightly to 218\par from 219 late Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the local money market, rates were mostly steady as liquidity\par remained sufficient in the banking system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                   Late Wednesday    Late Tuesday\par                   bid     offer     bid     offer\par Overnight         0.5000% 0.6250%   0.5625% 0.6875%\par 3-Month           0.7500% 0.8750%   0.7500% 0.8750%\par 1-Year            1.1250% 1.2500%   1.1250% 1.2500%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Izham Ahmad, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-64154-157;\par izham.ahmad@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020508dy58000mt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
