\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Buoyant, but cautious ahead of FOMC. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Anchalee Worrachate \par \uc2 735 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2002\par 12:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 7 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were on a \par \par \uc2  roll on Tuesday, holding strong gains against the dollar, \par \par \uc2  although some paused in late trade ahead of a U.S. Federal \par \par \uc2  Reserve meeting later in the day just in case there was a \par \par \uc2  surprise rate rise. \par \par \uc2      The market expects the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep its \par \par \uc2  federal funds rate steady at 1.75 percent for now, given recent \par \par \uc2  poor economic data and disappointing corporate earnings. \par \par \uc2      "Our view is that the dollar will continue to weaken, and \par \par \uc2  that meant Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are going to continue to strengthen \par \par \uc2  against the dollar on a trend basis," said Peter Redward, \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2      CAUTIOUS ABOUT CENTRAL BANKS \par \par \uc2      Buying of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also slowed by concerns of \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap gains against the dollar, \par \par \uc2  which some see as a threat to Asia's fragile economic recovery. \par \par \uc2      The Singapore dollar strengthened past the key 1.80 level \par \par \uc2  for the first time since October, but then pared gains on talk \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore might have been buying \par \par \uc2  dollars. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     At 0930 GMT, the Sing dollar        was at 1.8040, compared\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the intraday high of 1.7980.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Korean won         -2 finished at 1,279.50 per dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -- its highest level since December 13, when it ended at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,274.60.     The won was boosted by dollar weakness and higher\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interest rates, which make it more attractive to hold. The Bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of Korea on Tuesday surprised the market with a 25 basis point\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rate hike.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the won could have ended higher but there were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht rose against the dollar, but failed to break\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par convincingly above a key barrier of 42.85, despite the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  saying the baht's current level posed no threat to exports\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and that it would not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to depress the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "But that does not stop the market from being cautious. The\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par truth is the baht is heavily overbought against the dollar, and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par we have seen the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market lately, whether\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par they called it an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or not," said a dealer in\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  happy to talk up its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which said it saw the peso stabilising\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 48 to 49 to the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso closed higher at 49.64 against 49.775 on Monday,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with hefty turnover of $257.20 million. Exporters were selling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars on views the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's upside is limited for now.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. DOLLAR GLUM\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Asian rises reflected broad-based U.S. dollar weakness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par It hit multi-month lows against the yen, the euro and the Swiss\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par franc, on doubts over the U.S. economic outlook, shaky asset\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par markets and poor corporate earnings.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Wall Street stocks sank on Monday, with the Dow Jones\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par industrial average shedding almost 200 points.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Some analysts see the dollar's slide as part of much-needed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par correction, and expect it to regain ground in the medium term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The market is way too short of the dollar now, therefore a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strong upside potential is there," said a senior dealer at a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. bank in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "And with so much having been loaded into the pipelines,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the U.S. economy should recover well this year. Its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par productivity is still high. I think the market is just looking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for an excuse to take profits," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0943 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     127.64       127.48         -0.13\par  Sing dlr      1.8040       1.8060         +0.11\par  Taiwan dlr    34.565       34.565         +0.00\par  Korean won   1279.50      1281.20         +0.11\par  Baht           42.86        43.05         +0.44\par  Peso           49.61        49.78         +0.33\par  Rupiah       9285.00      9295.00         +0.11\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     127.64       131.24         +2.82\par  Sing dlr      1.8040       1.8515         +2.63\par  Korean won   1279.40      1277.00         -0.19\par  Baht           42.86        44.16         +3.03\par  Peso           49.61        51.50         +3.81\par  Rupiah       9285.00     10350.00        +11.47\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020507dy5700kdi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
