\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore dollar hits seven-month high. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Anchalee Worrachate \par \uc2 638 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2002\par 06:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 7 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar strengthened on Tuesday past the key 1.8000 level for the first time since October last year, after a firmer yen encouraged investors to add the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to their positions and cut losses on the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  A U.S. name and one major European bank were seen actively selling the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  versus the Sing, dealers said. At 0110 GMT, the Sing dollar was trading at 1.7998 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar tends to track the yen because of heavy trade flows between the two countries. Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  monitors the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's progress against a trade weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a managed float. The yen is believed to account for 15 percent of the basket. \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar, which has gained almost three percent so far this year from 1.8515 to the dollar, has been on a steady upward trend against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since early April. \par \par \uc2  "There are good bids for the Sing dollar this morning, mostly because of the yen's strength and the dollar's weakness. The U.S. asset markets don't look that attractive at the moment, and that should continue to add to selling pressure," said a dealer at a European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "The Fed meeting later in the day will be a non event, I think. People in the market appear to be convinced it will keep the rate steady," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht and the Philippine peso and the Korean won -2 hit fresh multi-month highs on Monday as market sentiment continued to go against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The baht was trading around 42.85 to the dollar, the peso at 49.50 and the won at 1,279.60. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  THREAT? \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists were divided over whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS), would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at current levels to meet its aim of a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The MAS actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stave off excessive volatility. \par \par \uc2  Some strategists expect the MAS to buy U.S. dollars soon, based on a view that the Singapore's economic recovery is still too fragile to warrant a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the 1.8000 level was a line of defence for now. \par \par \uc2  Others argued the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to leave the market alone for now because the Sing's dollar gains are in line with other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region. \par \par \uc2  "I don't see the MAS coming into the market before 1.7900, and that's almost another 100 points to go," said Peter Redward, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists at Deutsche Bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "In this environment where the yen and the euro are rising and Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are rising, I think the MAS will be cautious about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  too aggressively," he said. \par \par \uc2  U.S. DOLLAR BLEAK \par \par \uc2  The Asian rises reflected a falling U.S. dollar across the board. It hit multi-month lows against the yen, the euro and the Swiss franc, thanks to a sinking feeling over the U.S. economic outlook, shaky asset markets and poor corporate earnings. \par \par \uc2  Wall Street stocks sank on Monday, with the Dow Jones industrial average shedding almost 200 points as pessimism deepened. \par \par \uc2  But some analysts see the dollar's slide as part of much-needed correction, and expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to regain ground in a medium term. \par \par \uc2  "The market is way too short of the dollar now, therefore a strong upside potential is there," said a senior dealer at a U.S. bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "And with so much having been loaded into the pipelines, the U.S. economy should recover well this year. Its productivity is still high. I think the market is just looking for an excuse to take profits," he said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020507dy570086y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
