\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Edging higher, U.S. dollar defensive. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Anchalee Worrachate \par \uc2 775 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 April 2002\par 05:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, April 25 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  firmer across the broad on Thursday after the U.S. dollar was \par \par \uc2  put on the defensive by bleak economic data and the Federal \par \par \uc2  Reserve's "beige book", which pointed to muted recovery. \par \par \uc2      But after trading around their multi-week highs for a \par \par \uc2  while, most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  found themselves a bit top heavy, with \par \par \uc2  bargain hunters gradually snatching back dollars. \par \par \uc2      "The market is focused on the U.S. growth story, which \par \par \uc2  doesn't look very good at the moment," said Thio Chin Loo, \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas in Singapore. \par \par \uc2      "Meanwhile other countries such as the Euroland have come \par \par \uc2  up with some good numbers. That gives some thoughts to the \par \par \uc2  market that perhaps they should diversify from the U.S. dollar \par \par \uc2  to other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Thio. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar        was among star performers, rising by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a quarter of a percent as those economic concerns prompted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par traders to liquidate long dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dollar buying from some U.S. names and U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par demand linked to hedging activities by local firms capped the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sing dollar's gain at 1.8125 -- its five-month high.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht        was higher, briefly breaking above its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week high of 43.20 only to retrace on fears of cental bank\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and concerns over recent selling of local stocks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by foreign investors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It drew support from news that the government had raised\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its economic growth forecast for 2002 to 3.6 percent from 3.4\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent seen in March, although some economists see the number\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as too optimistic.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     U.S. ECONOMY STUTTERS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar was clouded by durable goods and new home sales\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par data which showed the U.S. economy has lost steam after growing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at a speedy pace earlier this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Buying orders for costly manufactured goods dropped 0.6\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in March while new homes sales fell 3.1 percent in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par same month, selling at an annual rate of 878,000, below the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forecast 882,000 pace.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dealers said what upset the market most was the Fed's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par beige book which is its anecdotal summary of economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par conditions across the country.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The report said the labor market was still "slack" and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par manufacturers' plans to invest in new equipment were "limited."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     WON, PESO RISE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won, which trailed the yen closely, made good gains. It\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was trading around 1,299 to the dollar at 0300 GMT compared\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with 1310.0 at the open and 1,307.0 at Wednesday's close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said barring \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the won might close above 1,300 for the first\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par time since December 19.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippine peso        lurched higher on the regionals'\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par coat tail as interbank players bought the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cover short positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "But we do expect some corporate players to buy the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at around 50.80," said a local dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     At 0300 GMT, the peso was trading around 50.82 with $54\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million transacted so far in the onshore market. It closed at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 50.895 on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategists expect appreciation in the regional\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to slow from here given recent foreign selling in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local stocks, which prompted concerns over potential outflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors sold a net 299.38 million baht ($6.92\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million) worth of Thai shares and 60.50 billion won ($46.67) in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Korean shares on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Given what is happening in the U.S. equity market, I think\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the stock markets around the region will find their tops pretty\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par soon. If the stocks take a breather, the dollar/Asians should\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par find a floor - meaning Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will come off," said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BNP's Thio.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0139 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     129.50       129.92         +0.32\par  Sing dlr      1.8150       1.8178         +0.15\par  Taiwan dlr    34.778       34.808         +0.09\par  Korean won   1299.00      1307.00         +0.60\par  Baht           43.23        43.30         +0.16\par  Peso           50.86        50.90         +0.08\par  Rupiah       9260.00      9310.00         +0.54\par  Ringgit       3.8000       3.7995         -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     129.50       131.24         +1.34\par  Sing dlr      1.8150       1.8515         +2.01\par  Taiwan dlr    34.778       32.900         -5.40\par  Korean won   1297.00      1277.00         -1.54\par  Baht           43.23        44.16         +2.15\par  Peso           50.86        51.50         +1.27\par  Rupiah       9260.00     10350.00        +11.77\par  Ringgit       3.8000       3.7995         -0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020425dy4p006mx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
