\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  -  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  dither on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 751 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2002\par 11:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , April 23 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  took \par \par \uc2  a step back from multi-week gains late Tuesday as dollar-buying \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears prompted players to cover their short dollar \par \par \uc2  positions. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts said despite a firmer yen       , holding strong\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par above 130 level, a slight trade-weighted appreciation of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar was seen as raising chances of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aimed at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par capping exchange rate gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar trade-weighted index        rose to a high of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 116.82, up from late Monday's 116.49. The United States is the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par biggest export market for most Asian economies.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Some of these regionals have come quite far, quite quickly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and now there is a bit of a sense of some restraint creeping\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in," said David Simmonds, Salomon Smith Barney's strategist in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Simmonds said the latest economic data indicated, at best,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a gradual recovery in most regional economies and the U.S., but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par there is lingering suspicion on the yen's recent run up.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "So from this stage onwards both policy makers and markets\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par are likely to look for some restraint...though there might\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par still be some more room for gains in some of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     WEAK BIAS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was already spotted in the market,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as usual, capping Taiwan dollar's gains after it got\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par near four-month highs at around 34.76 per dollar, backed by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par continuing equity-related dollar inflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai Baht        was slightly weaker on dollar-buying\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fears exacerbated after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 14-day repurchase rate unchanged at 2.0 percent, signalling it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par favours a relatively weaker baht to boost growth and exports\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over loose monetary conditions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht eased to around 43.30 per dollar from late Monday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 's 43.25.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE RUMOURS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In Singapore, dollar offers from two local banks sparked\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rumours they were acting on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Singapore dollar strengthened to five and a half\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par month highs around 1.8125.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However most dealers said they found no evidence supporting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the rumours and argued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risks were low unless the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sing dollar challenges 1.8100 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Technical analysts said the market would need fresh impetus\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to take out a strong 200-day moving average dollar/Sing support\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at around 1.8123. But a convincing breach of that level could\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par send the Sing dollar to levels beyond 1.8100, they added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MORE PATIENT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the Bank of Korea was expected to be more\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par patient as a stronger won -2 may induce some monetary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tightening, need to keep a lid on inflationary growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won touched a high of 1,303.9, a level not seen since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par January 7, as offshore players and exporters offloaded dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, concerns over equity-related dollar outflows pulled it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par back to late Monday's levels around 1,306.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par DIFFERENT REASONS FOR RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For different reasons, the Indonesian rupiah also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par eased beyond the 9,300 per dollar level after hitting fresh\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par seven month highs around 9,240 early on.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Jakarta said a rupiah liquidity squeeze due to a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporate tax payment deadline forced players to cover their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, the widely-expected sovereign credit rating\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par downgrade to "selective default" by Standard & Poor's had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par little impact on the rupiah.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said S&P had been telegraphing the move for weeks,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par linking it to a recent $5.4 billion foreign debt rescheduling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deal with the Paris Club of creditor nations under which some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par private loans would also be affected.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.       $0852 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     129.96       130.11         +0.12\par  Sing dlr      1.8186       1.8172         -0.08\par  Taiwan dlr    34.810       34.845         +0.10\par  Korean won   1298.80      1302.20         +0.26\par  Baht           43.28        43.25         -0.07\par  Peso           50.96        50.95         -0.01\par  Rupiah       9360.00      9250.00         -1.18\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     129.96       131.24         +0.98\par  Sing dlr      1.8186       1.8515         +1.81\par  Taiwan dlr    34.810       34.986         +0.51\par  Korean won   1298.80      1277.00         -1.68\par  Baht           43.28        44.16         +2.03\par  Peso           50.96        51.50         +1.07\par  Rupiah       9360.00     10350.00        +10.58\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020423dy4n00ius\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
