\par\par \b \uc2  Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Up Late; NT$ Hits 4-Month High \b0\par\par\uc2  By Alan Yonan Jr. \par \uc2 804 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 2002\par 11:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Several Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  posted near-term highs Monday as prospects for economic recovery in the region continued to damp the dollar's popularity. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar and Indonesian rupiah recorded their best performances so far this year. The South Korean won, Singapore dollar and Thai baht also strengthened, but the Philippine peso tumbled following a bomb explosion that killed 14 people Sunday in the southern part of the country. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tried to keep a lid on the New Taiwan dollar's rise by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  still managed to power its way to a four-month closing high against its U.S. counterpart. \par \par \uc2  Foreign inflows to the local stock market, which surged to NT$35 billion last week, have been helping fuel demand for the New Taiwan dollar. \par \par \uc2  Although the normally \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has eased its activity in the market in recent days, it jumped in and bought U.S. dollars when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell through several key support levels on its way to an intraday low of NT$34.757. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought an estimated US$600 million to US$700 million, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped the U.S. dollar recover some of its losses to close at NT$34.845, down from $34.898 Friday. It was the New Taiwan dollar's best finish since Dec. 20 when it closed at NT$34.756. \par \par \uc2  For most of this year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has managed the New Taiwan dollar in a fairly tight trading range in an effort to keep the country's exports competitive with the likes of Korea and Singapore, said James Malcolm, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan. The pair has traded roughly between NT$35.10 and NT$34.90. \par \par \uc2  But with signs of economic recovery beginning to lift other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region, Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is apparently more willing to let the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthen against the dollar, he said. \par \par \uc2  "Going forward we expect authorities to become more comfortable with letting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  go higher," he said. \par \par \uc2  JP Morgan is forecasting the U.S. dollar to weaken to NT$34.50 by the end of June and NT$33.50 by the end of the year, Malcolm said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The rupiah powered to its best finish since last September,\par continuing a rally that began last month with the government's\par successful sale of its 51% stake in PT Bank Central Asia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar closed at 9,255 rupiah, down from IDR9,340 Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With political stability and economic reforms helping reduce the risk\par sometimes associated with Indonesia, investors are becoming more\par attracted by the high yields Indonesian assets have to offer, JP\par Morgan's Malcolm said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said he expects the rupiah, which has already appreciated by 10% to\par 12% so far this year, to strengthen to about IDR8,500 per dollar by the\par end of the year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won ended at a three-month high, but came off its intraday peak on\par late afternoon dollar demand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar finished at 1,308.8 won, down from Friday's close of\par KRW1,312.3. It was the dollar's weakest finish since closing at\par KRW1,302.0 Jan. 7.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Demand for the dollar from corporations and offshore players pulled\par the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  off its morning low, sparking short covering at\par KRW1,307, said dealers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar rose to a six-week high, benefiting from the U.S.\par dollar selling going on elsewhere in the region.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Near the end of Asian trading the U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.8177,\par down from S$1.8221 late Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Heavy selling briefly pushed the U.S. dollar to a six-week low of\par S$1.8160 in mid-afternoon trading, but it bounced off the low amid fears\par the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  do prevent the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par dollar from strengthening too rapidly, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso was unable to overcome negative sentiment associated with a\par series of bomb explosions in the south.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar closed at 50.970 pesos on the Philippine Dealing System, up\par from PHP50.890 Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A series of bombings Sunday in General Santos, one of the largest\par cities in the southern Philippines, killed at least 14 people and\par injured around 45 others.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Another explosion occurred in General Santos early Monday, prompting\par President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo to order a state of emergency in the\par city.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht tracked other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Late in Asia the dollar was quoted at 43.260 baht, down from THB43.310\par late Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Alan Yonan Jr., Dow Jones Newswires; 65 9862-0905;\par alan.yonan@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020422dy4m000px\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
