\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Up Late; Taiwan Dlr Rises To 4-Mo High \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2 835 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 2002\par 11:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- After having been trapped in watertight ranges for months, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fragility against the yen and foreign equity inflows finally set the New Taiwan dollar free, propelling it to a four-month closing high Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , too, retained their recent strength, as the U.S. dollar remained on the defensive in international \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  But their gains were somewhat restrained by the yen's inability to make much more headway, as caution reigned ahead of this weekend's Washington meeting of finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors of the Group of Seven industrialized nations. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders are seeking clues from finance ministers on whether they will tolerate a weaker yen - as part of Japan's efforts to revive its ailing economy, participants said. \par \par \uc2  "We have no idea where the general dollar is going, especially against the yen," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0930 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y130.29, above Y129.86 in New York, but below Y130.61 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won and the Singapore dollar - which had been leading the region's advance in the past few sessions - turned instead to the New Taiwan dollar for direction Friday. \par \par \uc2  Foreign banks sold the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the New Taiwan dollar on the offshore non-deliverable forward market, amid persistent foreign equity inflows into Taipei and following the U.S. dollar's temporary slide below Y130. \par \par \uc2  "The morning's moves were very speculative," said a dealer in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar muscled through key resistance at NT$34.900 against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's closure below that level signals Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's willingness to allow the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate further - albeit in a controlled fashion - if the yen trends higher and portfolio inflows persist, observers said. \par \par \uc2  Still, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check on any excessive strength in New Taiwan dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In the last 15 minutes of trade, US$372 million changed hands, pulling the New Taiwan dollar off the NT$34.858 level against the U.S. dollar, dealers in Taipei noted. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar closed at NT$34.898 against its U.S. counterpart, stronger than NT$34.940 Thursday. The New Taiwan dollar touched an intraday high of NT$34.838. \par \par \uc2  Trading volume more than doubled to US$1.41 billion - the highest daily volume since early August - from US$632 million Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Charts suggest that the U.S. dollar may be entering a weaker medium-term range of NT$34.70-NT$34.90. \par \par \uc2  Judging by bearish daily oscillators, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could test immediate support at NT$34.79 - which marks a 50% retracement of its move up in December - with the permission of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that is. \par \par \uc2  Bank of America believes Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to maintain its vigil on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - even as it allows it to appreciate slightly. \par \par \uc2  "The Taiwanese authority is not very sure about this recovery," said Bank of America's Hong Kong-based analyst, Steven Cheung. "It wants to wait for a solid recovery, which will probably take place in the second half, before allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate dramatically." \par \par \uc2  Foreign institutional investors bought a net NT$2.14 billion of shares on the Taiwan Stock Exchange Friday, the exchange said. For the month to date, foreign institutional investors have bought a net NT$38.03 billion of shares. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  found support from foreign equity inflows and the yen to close at a three-month high, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 1,312.2 won, down from KRW1,313.2 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors were net buyers of KRW130.9 billion of South Korean shares, as they extended their buying spree since Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Tracking the yen and the New Taiwan dollar, the Singapore dollar climbed to a five-week high of S$1.8188 against its U.S. counterpart, before relinquishing part of its gains, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 1000 GMT (6:00 a.m. EDT), the Singapore dollar was quoted at S$1.8226, stronger than S$1.8235 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Following the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's inexhorable rise of late, fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the local \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  have crept in, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There's a feeling that if the U.S. dollar falls further to S$1.8150, it could attract the attention of the authority because the slide has been sharp recently," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  On the Philippine Dealing System, the dollar closed at 50.890 pesos, down from PHP50.940 Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at 43.329 baht to the dollar, slightly firmer compared with THB43.310 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4043; netty.ismail@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020419dy4j000so\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
