\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asian  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  ride yen's coattails higher. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,064 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2002\par 03:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, April 10 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose \par \par \uc2  early on Wednesday, riding on the yen's coattails. \par \par \uc2      Concerns about the Middle East, where the Israeli army \par \par \uc2  reported its highest number of casualties so far in its \par \par \uc2  conflict with the Palestinians, hounded the dollar. Investors \par \par \uc2  ran for the safe cover of other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of \par \par \uc2  worries that U.S. involvement in the Middle East and rising oil \par \par \uc2  prices could hamper the country's economy. \par \par \uc2  But the gains in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were modest because of \par \par \uc2  local developments and most of Asia's susceptibility to any \par \par \uc2  rises in oil prices, not only from the Palestinian-Israeli \par \par \uc2  conflict but also from the possibility that the United States \par \par \uc2  may strike at Iraq in the next stage of its war on terror. \par \par \uc2  "East Asia ex-Japan is particularly sensitive to oil price \par \par \uc2  fluctuation. The region imported six million barrels per day in \par \par \uc2  2000. Each dollar increase in oil price would amount to 0.1% of \par \par \uc2  GDP in extra cost," said Andy Xie, chief economist at Morgan \par \par \uc2  Stanley Dean Witter in Hong Kong, in a research note. \par \par \uc2  Malaysia and Indonesia are Asia's only net oil exporters. \par \par \uc2  On the local front, advance figures for Singapore's first \par \par \uc2  quarter gross domestic product showed the economy shrank more \par \par \uc2  than expected by 2.6 percent on the year. But analysts said the \par \par \uc2  city-state's recovery was still on track. \par \par \uc2      Taiwan will issue its March exports and trade balance data \par \par \uc2  at 0800 GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won opened slightly lower before creeping up on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par back of the yen's rebound. It kicked off a trading session at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1,330.60 compared with the Tuesday's closing of 1,329.60, but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par later rose to 1,328.60.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was top heavy due to recent foreign selling of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local stocks which sparked concern of outflows. In April, net\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign equity outflows from Korea was recorded at $1.9 million\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as of April 3.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Concerns over the lingering Middle East conflict and its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par potential impact on oil prices also weighed on the won because\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Korea is a major net oil importer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Although the yen/won cross has risen to around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10 from around 9.8 last week, some strategists continue to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par suggest that clients stick to short yen/won positions as the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pair is likely to fall to around 9.0-9.5 by mid-year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar is trading higher, drawing support from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains in the yen which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  closely trails, and hopes\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for more inflows into the equity market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  opened at 34.952 from 34.982 at the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close in the previous session.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     According to JP Morgan, net equity inflows into Taiwan as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of April 3 were US$1.5 million. The inflows in the first\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quarter were recorded at US$2.02 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar lost some ground after first quarter\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gross domestic product data failed to impress the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Local banks and interbank players bought U.S. dollars at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 1.8350 pushing up the Sing dollar to 1.8370, but dealers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to remain rangebound.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     First quarter Singapore GDP figures fell towards the bottom\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par end of forecasts validating long dollar positions, dealers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Advance figures were down 2.6 percent on year. The market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par had expected a contraction of between 1.8-2.5 percent. The\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economy shrank 6.6 percent in the fourth quarter last year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht edged higher with gains in the yen and other\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regionals giving the market confidence that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap its rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Moreover, dealers in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said foreign names were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par still spotted selling dollars as the baht strengthened beyond\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the 43.50 per dollar level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht had recently seen upside pressure on equity and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investment related inflows with sentiment buoyed by hopes of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economic recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But with exports still struggling the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par repeatedly hinted that it would like to keep the baht at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par relatively weaker levels.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINES PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso poked above the 51 level aided by thin demand for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, a lack of fresh leads and a firmer regional bias.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Manila said dollar bids by local corporates were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected to be lined up around 50.80-50.90 level while offers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were expected around 51.10.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said with no strong enough fresh factors the peso may\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par continue to stay within a tight range around the 51 per U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar level for the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah lost its footing against the U.S. dollar, and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was clinging to the 9,600 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     After several sessions of steady gains, the rupiah ran into\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local corporate dollar demand that forced it to beat a retreat.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Still, charts showed the dollar/rupiah consolidating around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par these levels rather than reversing its recent uptrend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Indeed, dealers in Jakarta said many players were looking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to sell the dollar on rally with sentiment towards the rupiah\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par still upbeat ahead of key Paris Club talks on Thursday and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Jakarta is seeking to reschedule $5.5 billion in debt due\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par between April 2002 and December 2003. While the government has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expressed confidence un securing the deal, a senior Japanese\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Finance Ministry official warned Jakarta on Tuesday against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par seeking very generous terms, saying it would hurt confidence\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par among private lenders.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0137 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     130.73       131.61         +0.67\par  Sing dlr      1.8333       1.8383         +0.27\par  Taiwan dlr    34.948       34.982         +0.10\par  Korean won   1328.60      1329.50         +0.07\par  Baht           43.46        43.52         +0.14\par  Peso           51.01        51.06         +0.09\par  Rupiah       9605.00      9585.00         -0.21\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     130.73       131.24         +0.39\par  Sing dlr      1.8333       1.8515         +0.99\par  Taiwan dlr    34.948       34.986         +0.11\par  Korean won   1328.60      1313.00         -1.17\par  Baht           43.46        44.16         +1.61\par  Peso           51.01        51.50         +0.96\par  Rupiah       9605.00     10350.00         +7.76\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020410dy4a003ei\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
